{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1B4h2LTaRUTikqyfUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MT2P86bbnRDv1NAsMkmp3j","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":470,"limit":450},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14985,"cache_read_input_tokens":24515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14985},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b392508-0a9c-4851-a1e8-b9fce2e4b886","uuid":"cc1b9a2c-2cb9-43cd-b2f0-0ba3d83516dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:56:34.617Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1B4NSGRYE8TMDBccAa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MT2P86bbnRDv1NAsMkmp3j":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":470,"limit":450}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MT2P86bbnRDv1NAsMkmp3j","type":"tool_result","content":"470\t```\n471\tintro → kickoff → play ⇄ (tackle → ruck → play)\n472\t                       ⇄ (knockOn | forwardPass → scrum → play)\n473\t                       ⇄ (touch → lineout → play)\n474\t                       ⇄ (foul → [advantage] → penalty → choice → setKick | tapGo | kickToTouch→lineout)\n475\t                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n476\t          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n477\t          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\n478\thooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n479\t```\n480\t\n481\t- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n482\t  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n483\t  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n484\t- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n485\t  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n486\t- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n487\t- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n488\t  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n489\t- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n490\t\n491\t### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n492\t\n493\t- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n494\t  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n495\t  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n496\t- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n497\t  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n498\t- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n499\t  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n500\t- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n501\t  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n502\t  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n503\t- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n504\t  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n505\t  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n506\t- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n507\t  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n508\t  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n509\t    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n510\t    ground.\n511\t  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n512\t    seat colour.\n513\t\n514\t### 7.3 The ball\n515\t\n516\t- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n517\t  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n518\t- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) updated with the map, so it bounces off the stands'\n519\t  walls as the sports kit's ball does off its boards (on the field there are no walls: out of play is decided by the\n520\t  lines, below); air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s; wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne.\n521\t- **The oval bounce** (the soul of loose-ball chaos): on each ground contact with vertical speed above 30, rotate its\n522\t  ground velocity by `±U(0, 70°) × bounceChaos` and scale its rebound height by `U(0.3, 1.25)`; a grubber bounces\n523\t  higher at random (\"sat up nicely\"); all from `TT.rng`. Spin (end over end for kicks, spiral for passes) is drawn from\n524\t  `ball.rot`.\n525\t- Out of play: the ball's centre crossing a touchline (or the carrier's feet touching one) is **touch** → lineout to the\n526\t  team that did not touch it last, at the x where it crossed (moved 51 u from the try lines). Crossing a dead-ball line\n527\t  or touch-in-goal: if the attackers put it there → **22 drop-out** to the defenders; if the defenders did and it was\n528\t  not a kick from in-goal → 5 m scrum to the attackers.\n529\t- Pick-up: a loose ball below z 9 within 9 u of a player whose state accepts it (and 4.5 u if it moves faster than\n530\t  210) is gathered; at full sprint 15% are fumbled forward (a knock-on) unless HND ≥ 8.\n531\t\n532\t### 7.4 Passing\n533\t\n534\t- **Who receives:** legal receivers are teammates not in front of the passer (`(rx - px) × dir ≤ 4`), within 220 u,\n535\t  standing and not binned. L1 picks among those above the passer (smaller y), R1 among those below. Tap: the nearest by\n536\t  `|dy|` within 110 u (short pass). Hold more than 0.25 s: the second-nearest on that side, or the nearest if he is the\n537\t  only one (long pass, 300 u/s).\n538\t- **Flight:** aim at the receiver's lead point `rx + rvx × t × 0.9` (t from distance / speed), launched with\n539\t  `E.arc(..., { apex: 6 })` for short, `apex: 10` long; 230 u/s short.\n540\t- **Catch:** in the receiver's 10 u reach and below z 30: chance = `catchBase × (0.9 + 0.01 × HND)`, minus 0.06 for a\n541\t  long pass, minus `pressurePenalty` (0.12) with a defender within 20 u, minus 0.06 in rain; Grease Jersey and Iron\n542\t  Shoulders do not change it; a pass from or to a player ON FIRE is always caught. A miss either drops forward\n543\t  (knock-on) or spills loose (50/50 by the ball's direction).\n544\t- **Forward pass:** judged as the law does, relative to the passer: if `(ball velocity - passer velocity) · dir > 4\n545\t  u/s` at release, it is forward. The referee always calls it (whistle when caught or grounded): scrum to the other\n546\t  team. Only a mouse click on a man in front (or no assist) can throw one; the hover shows it red first.\n547\t- **Dummy:** a pass button with no legal receiver on that side (and pass assist off, or nobody anywhere) is a dummy:\n548\t  the carrier sells it; each defender within 40 u with eyes on the carrier \"buys it\" with 40% (turns toward the fake\n549\t  receiver for 0.3 s); +4 hype per defender sold.\n550\t- **Offload:** within the first 0.15 s of being tackled (not a big hit), L1/R1 pops a short pass to a legal receiver\n551\t  within 50 u; catch chance -0.1; +6 hype.\n552\t- **Interception:** a pass that flies within 10 u of an opponent below z 24 can be taken: the CPU tries with\n553\t  `0.15 × interceptMult`; a human holding ✕ near the lane (within 12 u) tries with 0.45. Success: the ball and +12 hype,\n554\t  and usually a long run.\n555\t\n556\t### 7.5 Running moves\n557\t\n558\t- **Sidestep (✕ with the ball):** an impulse of `sidestepPower` (140 u/s) perpendicular to the run toward the stick's\n559\t  side (no stick: away from the nearest defender), for `sidestepEvade` (0.25 s) any tackle attempt whiffs; cooldown\n560\t  0.6 s. A whiffed tackler stumbles (0.5 s). +6 hype when it beats a committed tackler.\n561\t- **Spin (✕ twice within 0.25 s):** 0.4 s evade, a full 360° body spin, 15% speed loss after; beats big hits too.\n562\t- **Fend (□ with the ball):** opens a 0.3 s `fendWindow` (the stiff arm out). A standard tackle arriving inside it\n563\t  fails with `fendBeat` (0.7) + 0.03 × (carrier POW - tackler TKL); a big hit fails with half that. A beaten tackler\n564\t  is shoved back 20 u and sits down (0.8 s). Cooldown 0.8 s. +6 hype.\n565\t- **Line break:** the carrier gets past the defensive line (every opponent but at most one, the deep sweeper, is now\n566\t  behind him, nearer his own try line): banner \"LINE BREAK!\", +8 hype, support runners turbo.\n567\t- **Grounding a try:** in the in-goal, ✕ dives and grounds (with style: +3 hype); otherwise the ball is grounded by\n568\t  itself after 2.5 s in the in-goal, when within 16 u of the dead-ball line, or when tackled there (always a try,\n569\t  arcade law). Running toward the posts before grounding makes the conversion easier: a real decision with the clock\n570\t  and the chasers.\n571\t\n572\t### 7.6 Kicking\n573\t\n574\t- **Grubber (tap ○):** along the ground 140-200 u ahead (stick aims within ±45°), `vz` 40, extra bounce chaos.\n575\t- **Punt (hold ○, release):** the meter fills in 0.9 s; while it fills the carrier runs straight on and the stick only\n576\t  aims. Distance `lerp(120, kickMax (520), power) × (0.75 + 0.03 × KCK)`; apex 60-110; aimed by the stick (forward\n577\t  cone ±70°; no stick: straight). Over 0.9 of the meter is the \"sweet spot\": +8% distance and true flight; outside, a\n578\t  random hook of up to ±(11 - KCK)°.\n579\t- **Bomb / up-and-under (punt with the stick pulled back at release):** apex 150, distance × 0.5; it hangs, and chasers\n580\t  can contest the catch (§7.11).\n581\t- **Kick to touch:** any punt aimed across a touchline goes out where it crosses: lineout to the other team (or to the\n582\t  kicking team from a penalty, §7.12).\n583\t- **Drop goal (hold ○ inside the opponents' 22, or within 300 u of their posts and facing them):** aimed at the posts\n584\t  (the stick nudges it ±8°); power and accuracy as a punt; good if it passes between the uprights above the crossbar:\n585\t  3 points. In that zone the stick pulled back at release still gives a bomb, and the stick pushed toward a touchline\n586\t  a cross-field punt; otherwise a held kick is the drop goal (the prompt says so: \"{b:ci} HOLD: DROP GOAL\").\n587\t- **Mouse:** right button hold and release kicks toward the cursor; the landing ring is drawn where it will come down at\n588\t  the current fill; the kind follows the same rules (in their 22 facing the posts: a drop goal).\n589\t- A landing marker (a pulsing ring decal) shows where every kick will come down, for both teams.\n590\t\n591\t### 7.7 Tackling\n592\t\n593\t- **Tackle (tap ✕ without the ball):** reaches 14 u (`tackleRange`) in front (within ±70° of facing). Chance =\n594\t  `tackleBase (0.78) × (0.9 + 0.02 × TKL - 0.02 × carrier POW)`, plus 0.1 from the side or behind, plus the\n595\t  difficulty bonus, minus 0.05 if the carrier is on turbo. Success: the paired `tackle` action (§11.2), then a ruck. Failure: \"broken\n596\t  tackle\": the tackler falls (0.6 s), the carrier staggers 0.4 s and goes on (+5 hype to the attack).\n597\t- **Big hit (hold ✕, let go in range):** charging takes `bigHitCharge` (0.7 s) to full; the charger moves at 1.15x and\n598\t  glows. Let go within 18 u: chance `0.7 + 0.2 × charge`. Full charge = **MONSTER HIT**: the carrier is launched\n599\t  (`bigHitLaunch`: 30-60 u back, z 20-40, a full flip), lands heavily and slides; the ball pops loose with\n600\t  `spillChance` (0.5), forward = knock-on; hit-stop 0.12 s, flash, shake 6, rumble, the crowd \"OOOOH\", a replay. Held\n601\t  past 1.2 s the charge goes red: a frontal hit then is a **high shot** (a foul, a yellow card if seen). A missed big\n602\t  hit sprawls the hitter for 1.0 s.\n603\t- **Dive tackle (□ without the ball):** a 0.35 s lunge of 30 u (`diveRange`); contact trips the carrier (an ankle tap:\n604\t  he falls forward, a tackle); a miss leaves the diver down for 1.2 s.\n605\t- **Gang tackle:** players with `immovable` (the boss, BIG UNIT; anyone in THUNDER RUN is simply unstoppable) are only\n606\t  \"held\" by the first successful tackle (they slow to 40% and drag the tackler); a second tackle within 1.0 s brings\n607\t  them down; otherwise they shrug it off after 1.2 s and the tackler is flung aside.\n608\t- **Cheap shot:** ✕ on an opponent without the ball (within 14 u) is a shoulder barge: the victim is flattened for\n609\t  1.6 s. It is a foul only if the referee sees it (§7.13). Unseen: +8 hype and Barry: \"The ref's missed that completely!\"\n610\t- **Collisions:** launched bodies hitting other players knock them down (1.0 s); hitting the referee is REF DOWN.\n611\t\n612\t### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n613\t\n614\t- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n615\t  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n616\t  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n617\t- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.2 + 0.1 ×\n618\t  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players. Mashing: a\n619\t  side with a human seat (its controlled player committed, or the tackled carrier) is driven by that seat's presses of\n620\t  ✕, each worth `mashWeight` (0.05), several humans adding up; a side with no human presses at `cpuMash` per second (±\n621\t  20%). Worked example, two attackers (POW 8 + 6) against one defender (POW 8): the commitment adds +0.12 a second, so a\n622\t  human who does not mash against a CPU at 9 presses a second ends at 0.3 + (0.12 - 0.45) × 1.6 = -0.23 (turnover); one\n623\t  mashing at 12 against a CPU at 6 ends at +0.97.\n624\t- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n625\t  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n626\t  foul if seen.\n627\t- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n628\t  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n629\t- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n630\t  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n631\t- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n632\t  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n633\t  draws the line.\n634\t\n635\t### 7.9 Scrum\n636\t\n637\t- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n638\t  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n639\t- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n640\t  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n641\t- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n642\t  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n643\t  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n644\t- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n645\t  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n646\t  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n647\t- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n648\t  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n649\t  (5 points, grounded at the scrum's y, so converted from in line with it).\n650\t\n651\t### 7.10 Lineout\n652\t\n653\t- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n654\t  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n655\t- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n656\t  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n657\t  couch play).\n658\t- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n659\t  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n660\t- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n661\t  chose another pod, the throwers win it. If they chose the same pod, their jumper contests: attack score = 0.6 ×\n662\t  throw quality (0-1, from the needle) + 0.04 × jumper HND + 0.15; defence score = 0.6 × timing (1 - |press - arrival|\n663\t  / 0.3, clamped 0-1, from ✕ pressed as the ball arrives) + 0.04 × jumper HND; the higher score takes it (\"STOLEN!\").\n664\t  The winner taps it down to his scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three\n665\t  times running); a CPU defence picks the right pod with its difficulty's read chance, and its timing error is drawn\n666\t  from its scrum timing σ.\n667\t\n668\t### 7.11 Kick-offs and 22 drop-outs\n669\t\n670\t- Kick-off from the centre spot by the fly-half (drop kick). The kicker aims a reticle (stick or mouse) on the\n671\t  receiving half and holds ○ (or the left mouse button) for power, letting go to kick. It must travel 102 u (\"10 m\"):\n672\t  short = \"NOT TEN!\" → a free kick to the receivers at halfway; straight into touch = a scrum to the receivers at\n673\t  halfway.\n674\t- Receivers catch automatically when the ball comes to a player in reach (10 u, z < 30). When a chaser and a receiver\n675\t  both reach a high ball, it's a **contest**: each presses ✕ as it arrives; the better timing (CPU: by difficulty and\n676\t  HND) takes it, the other is bumped down.\n677\t- 22 drop-out: the same, by the defending team from its own 22 line, distance unlimited.\n678\t\n679\t### 7.12 Tries, conversions, penalties, free kicks\n680\t\n681\t- **Try:** 5 points; celebration (each player has a celebration, §11.2), then a replay if earned (§7.20), then the\n682\t  conversion.\n683\t- **Conversion** (and **penalty goal**) set kick, in the behind-the-kicker camera:\n684\t  1. **Place:** move the tee back along the line through the grounding point parallel to touch (stick up/down, mouse\n685\t     drag or wheel), 51-400 u from the try line; the angle and the distance read out (\"38 M\").\n686\t  2. **Aim:** a reticle on the posts' plane, moved by the stick or the mouse; it sways a little (more for low KCK and\n687\t     higher difficulty); a windsock and arrow show the wind.\n688\t  3. **Power:** hold ○ (or the left mouse button) and let go: a meter needs to reach the distance's mark (shown); a\n689\t     tight accuracy band near the top adds no hook; elsewhere hooks up to ±(12 - KCK)°.\n690\t  4. **Flight:** the ball flies in 3D with the wind; it scores if it crosses the try line's plane between the uprights\n691\t     above the crossbar; hitting an upright is a DOINK (it bounces off, missed).\n692\t  A 20 s shot clock runs (the crowd's slow hand-clap speeds up). Conversion 2, penalty goal 3. CPU kicks are the same\n693\t  flight with an error drawn from its kicker's stats.\n694\t- **Penalty:** after a seen foul (and no advantage gained) the non-offending team's captain chooses on a big three-card\n695\t  screen (stick or mouse; CPU chooses by score, time and distance): **TAP & GO** (play restarts at once; the offenders\n696\t  are put 102 u back), **KICK AT GOAL** (if within 400 u; a set kick for 3), **KICK FOR TOUCH** (a punt aimed at the\n697\t  touchline; the kicking team throws in at the lineout).\n698\t- **Free kick** (early engagement, not ten): as a penalty, but no kick at goal.\n699\t- **Penalty try:** a seen foul against a carrier within 60 u of the try line with no defender between him and the line:\n700\t  7 points, no conversion.\n701\t\n702\t### 7.13 The referee and the laws he calls\n703\t\n704\t- **Referee Nigel Blewitt** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, whistle). He runs to a spot 50 u behind the ball on\n705\t  the attacking side and 40 u toward the far touchline (so he never stands between play and the camera), at 95 u/s,\n706\t  steering round players; he turns to face the ball at 4 rad/s. His eyes: `E.sees(ref, offender, { range: refRange\n707\t  (260), fov: refFov (1.4) })` at the moment of the foul and again 0.3 s later. A \"Show the ref's view\" setting (default\n708\t  on) draws his `r.sightCone` faintly on the grass: the over-the-top tactic of fouling behind his back is part of the\n709\t  game.\n710\t- Always called (they are not about being seen): forward pass, knock-on, touch, not straight, early engagement, use it.\n711\t- Called only if seen: **high shot** (an over-charged frontal big hit): penalty + yellow card; **cheap shot** (a hit on\n712\t  a player without the ball): penalty, a yellow card for the same player's second; **offside** (a defender ahead of his\n713\t  offside line closing on the ball within 30 u when it comes out of a ruck, scrum or lineout): penalty; **hands in the\n714\t  ruck**: penalty.\n715\t- **Advantage:** a seen foul by team A while team B has the ball or a loose ball near it: the referee calls ADVANTAGE B\n716\t  (arm out) and play goes on; if B gains 100 u or scores within 5 s, ADVANTAGE OVER; if B loses the ball or 5 s pass\n717\t  without gain, play comes back for the penalty at the mark.\n718\t- **Cards and the sin bin:** a yellow card sends the player to the sin bin (the dumpster on the touchline) for `sinBin`\n719\t  (30 s of running clock); his team plays with six; the AI shape adapts. A second yellow for the same player is a red\n720\t  card: off for the match. A banner, the ref's card held high, the crowd boos, and a sad trombone.\n721\t- **Ref down:** a launched body, the chicken or a flying bystander hitting the referee floors him for 8 s: no fouls are\n722\t  called at all (cards, offside, cheap shots all free), \"REF DOWN! ANYTHING GOES!\", then he gets up and play goes on.\n723\t- The referee's calls appear as speech balloons over him (\"CROUCH!\", \"BIND!\", \"SET!\", \"USE IT!\", \"ADVANTAGE!\", \"PLAY\n724\t  ON!\", \"HANDS AWAY!\", \"PENALTY!\", \"KNOCK ON!\", \"FORWARD!\", \"NOT STRAIGHT!\") with his babble voice and arm signals.\n725\t\n726\t### 7.14 Scoring\n727\t\n728\t| Score | Points |\n729\t|---|---|\n730\t| Try (and pushover try) | 5 |\n731\t| Conversion | 2 |\n732\t| Penalty goal | 3 |\n733\t| Drop goal | 3 |\n734\t| Penalty try | 7 |\n735\t\n736\t### 7.15 Hype and supers\n737\t\n738\t- A HYPE meter per team (0-100), shown on the score bug. Gains (× `hypeMult`): tackle 4, broken tackle 5, sidestep or\n739\t  fend that beats a man 6, dummy 4 per man sold, offload 6, line break 8, big hit 10, monster hit 16, interception 12,\n740\t  jackal or ruck turnover 8, scrum won 6, lineout steal 8, try 15, conversion 5, drop goal 10, unseen cheap shot 8, air\n741\t  horn 40.\n742\t- Full: \"△ SUPER!\" flashes on the meter and over the team's controlled players.\n743\t- **THUNDER RUN** (△ with the ball): `superTime` (4 s); the carrier is on fire, 1.35x speed, unstoppable (tacklers\n744\t  bounce off and fly like skittles), the ball cannot be knocked loose; ends on a pass, a kick, a try or time.\n745\t- **HURRICANE HIT** (△ without the ball): the controlled defender locks onto the carrier and homes in at 2x speed for\n746\t  up to 2 s; contact is a guaranteed monster hit with the ball loose and everyone within 30 u knocked over; if the ball\n747\t  is passed first, it re-targets the new carrier once.\n748\t- CPU teams use supers: Thunder Run in the opponents' half with space ahead; Hurricane Hit when the opposing carrier is\n749\t  within 120 u of their try line.\n750\t\n751\t### 7.16 ON FIRE\n752\t\n753\tA player who scores two tries in a row (no opposing score between) is ON FIRE until the other team scores or 90 s pass:\n754\tunlimited turbo, passes and catches never fail, fends ×1.5, tackles on him ×0.6, kicks +20% distance, a flame trail\n755\t(emissive), a music layer, \"HE'S ON FIRE!\".\n756\t\n757\t### 7.17 Power-ups (thrown on by the crowd)\n758\t\n759\tEvery `powerupEvery` (30 ± 10 s) of open play a fan in the stand throws one onto the pitch (an `E.arc` from the crowd\n760\tto a spot at least 80 u from the ball); one at a time; it stays 15 s (blinking for the last 3). The first player to run\n761\tover it takes it. The CPU diverts one off-ball player if it is within 100 u.\n762\t\n763\t| Power-up | Looks | Effect |\n764\t|---|---|---|\n765\t| MEAT PIE | a steaming pie in a foil tray | turbo refilled and unlimited for 6 s |\n766\t| IRON SHOULDERS | riveted shoulder pads | 15 s: his tackles and fends always win; his hits are monster hits |\n767\t| MEGA BOOT | a golden boot with wings | his team's next kick: ×1.6 distance, on fire; a set kick's accuracy band ×2 (60 s) |\n768\t| GREASE JERSEY | a glistening jersey | 8 s: tackles on him fail 70% |\n769\t| AIR HORN | a red air horn | +40 hype for his team at once; the crowd goes barmy |\n770\t\n771\t### 7.18 Venues: weather and hazards (one twist each; data in §9.2)\n772\t\n773\t| Venue | Weather | Hazard |\n774\t|---|---|---|\n775\t| Muddington Park | rain (0.7) | **mud** patches (4-6 floor-tag blobs): speed ×0.8, acceleration ×0.6, tackles +10%, ball skids; catches -6% in rain; kits get muddier as the match goes on (rig colours mixed toward brown by each player's time in mud and on the ground) |\n776\t| Port Grumble Docks | gusty wind | **wind** that shifts every 15-25 s (strength 0-1, a windsock on the HUD) pushes airborne balls (40 u/s² × strength × `windMult`); **CAPTAIN CLUCKY**, the giant chicken mascot, invades every 50-70 s, runs across on an `E.Path` for about 6 s, bowling over everyone in his way (the carrier drops the ball), chased by the referee |\n777\t| The Furnace | clear night | **flame jets**: grates 32 u inside each touchline (8 a side) erupt in sequences; each glows orange for 1.0 s (the warning), then burns for 1.2 s; anyone within 12 u is TOASTED (stunned 1.2 s, smoking, briefly blackened; a toasted carrier drops the ball); fireworks on every try |\n778\t| The Megadome | thunderstorm (rain 0.9) | **lightning** every 20-30 s: a crackling ring (36 u) warns for 1.4 s at a spot 60-200 u from the ball, then a strike: a flash, thunder, a scorch decal; anyone inside is stunned 1.5 s (drawn as a skeleton for two frames: a shared `build: 'skeleton'` rig drawn in their place) and a carrier inside drops the ball |\n779\t\n780\t`hazardEvery` (×1.0) scales every hazard's frequency; 0 turns them off.\n781\t\n782\t### 7.19 AI\n783\t\n784\tBoth CPU teams and the CPU teammates of humans run the same brain; difficulty and the team's style (§9.1) change its\n785\tnumbers, never its logic. Shapes are recomputed every 0.25 s per team (staggered); decisions every 0.15 s plus the\n786\treaction delay.\n787\t\n788\t- **Attack shape** (team in possession; carrier at `(cx, cy)`, attacking direction `d`): six support slots in a\n789\t  staggered line behind the carrier, three each side: slot k at `(cx - d × (18 + 10k), cy ∓ 44k)` (spacing 44 to the\n790\t  open side, 36 to the blind side), clamped 20 u inside touch. Forwards take the k = 1 slots, backs the wider ones, the\n791\t  wing the widest open-side slot; then nearest-first; a reassignment needs a 20 u improvement (hysteresis). Supporters\n792\t  never stand in front of the carrier (they check stride to stay 6 u behind). After a line break they turbo.\n793\t- **Defence shape:** a line at `cx + d × 30` facing the attack (behind the offside line when there is one), defenders\n794\t  paired to attackers by y order (\"man on man drift\") so the line slides with the attack; the nearest defender by\n795\t  intercept time is the **tackler** (aims at the carrier's predicted position), the second the **cover** (20 u behind\n796\t  and inside); the **sweeper** (the wing or fly-half) sits 140 u deep at `lerp(cy, CY, .5)` to field kicks, and joins\n797\t  the line when the ball is within 200 u of his try line. With six men (sin bin) the line spaces wider.\n798\t- **Tackler decisions:** in range and facing, after `aiReaction`: try with `0.6 + 0.3 × aggression`; a big hit if POW\n799\t  ≥ 7 or aggression ≥ 0.6 and the carrier is coming head on (charging from 40 u out); a dive tackle when chasing a\n800\t  faster carrier from 18-30 u behind; cheap shots on the nearest support runner when the referee is not looking, with\n801\t  the team's `cheapShots` rate.\n802\t- **Carrier decisions** (CPU carriers, and the human's teammates when they have the ball): score each option and take\n803\t  the best, with noise by difficulty: run forward (space in a 30° cone ahead), pass to each legal receiver (his space\n804\t  minus defenders near the lane), sidestep (a tackler committing within 22 u: 25% × skill), fend (a tackler within 16 u\n805\t  and POW ≥ 6: 40%), kick (deep in his own 22 under pressure: to touch; behind a flat line with a fast chaser: grubber\n806\t  or chip; the last 20 s, trailing by 3 or less, in range: drop goal), dive in the in-goal (or run to the posts when no\n807\t  defender is within 60 u). Steer toward the widest gap in the defensive line; keep 20 u inside touch; turbo in space\n808\t  and when racing to the line; keep 30% of the tank.\n809\t- **Loose ball:** the two nearest from each team chase its predicted rest point; the rest keep their shape.\n810\t- **Kicks:** the receiving team's nearest (or the sweeper) goes to the landing marker, a second supports; the kicking\n811\t  team's two fastest chase. (There is no offside in open play in this game; this is deliberate.)\n812\t- **Set pieces:** see each set piece above. CPU kick-offs aim short and contestable, 120-200 u past halfway toward a\n813\t  touchline. CPU penalty choice: kick at goal within 300 u when the score is close or late; kick to touch from far; tap\n814\t  & go within 50 u of the line or when trailing late.\n815\t- **Difficulty** (the player's Settings choice shifts each cup opponent one step):\n816\t\n817\t| | Rookie | Pro | Legend |\n818\t|---|---|---|---|\n819\t| `aiReaction` | 0.40 s | 0.25 s | 0.14 s |\n820\t| Tackle chance | -0.12 | 0 | +0.08 |\n821\t| `cpuMash` | 6/s | 9/s | 12/s |\n822\t| Decision noise | 0.35 | 0.20 | 0.08 |\n823\t| Interception × | 0.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n824\t| Scrum timing σ | 0.25 s | 0.12 s | 0.06 s |\n825\t| Early engagement | 8% | 3% | 0% |\n826\t| Lineout read | 0.25 | 0.35 | 0.45 |\n827\t\n828\t### 7.20 Instant replay\n829\t\n830\t- A ring buffer keeps the `MatchState` of the last 5 s at 60 Hz (every other step).\n831\t- Triggers: monster hits, supers, tries that came from a run of 200 u or more or beat a man, drop goals, pushover\n832\t  tries, interception tries; at most one replay in 30 s (tries always). Setting: Replays Big moments (default) / All\n833\t  tries / Off.\n834\t- Playback: the window from 2.5 s before to 1 s after the event, at 0.5x, through the normal presentation (states fed\n835\t  to the rigs), camera at zoom 1.35 on the key actor, letterbox bars, \"INSTANT REPLAY\" in the corner, Barry: \"Let's see\n836\t  that again!\"; any button skips. After a try it plays in the celebration, before the conversion. Never in AI Hub\n837\t  sessions.\n838\t\n839\t### 7.21 Stats and the Player of the Match\n840\t\n841\tPer team: possession % (time holding the ball), territory % (ball in the opponents' half), tries, conversions\n842\tmade/attempted, penalties conceded, tackles made/missed, big hits, monster hits, metres carried (`units / 10.24`), line\n843\tbreaks, turnovers won, offloads, cards. Player of the Match (winning side): tries × 10 + monster hits × 4 + tackles + metres\n844\t/ 10 + line breaks × 3 + turnovers × 3. Results show four tiles: TRIES, BIG HITS, METRES, POSSESSION.\n845\t\n846\t---\n847\t\n848\t## 8. Modes, scenes and flow\n849\t\n850\t```\n851\tboot → title ─(10 s idle)→ attract ─(any input)→ title\n852\t         │ PRESS START\n853\t         ▼\n854\t       menu ─(10 s idle)→ attract\n855\t         ├─ MEGA CUP ─→ cup hub ─→ story (prologue) → training (optional) → story (pre-match) → [join] → match\n856\t         │                 ▲                                                                        │\n857\t         │                 └──── results (win: next round; loss: CONTINUE? 10 s) ←───────────────────┘\n858\t         │                 final won → story (trophy) → story (third half) → credits → title\n859\t         ├─ EXHIBITION → join → setup (teams, venue, weather, time, halves) → match → results → rematch | menu\n860\t         ├─ TRAINING GROUND → drill list → match (drill) → next drill | list\n861\t         ├─ RECORDS → three tables (attract-style)\n862\t         ├─ SETTINGS → the standard settings screen (game.menu('settings'))\n863\t         └─ ABOUT & CREDITS → five pages\n864\tAI Hub session: boot → card (the game's own) → match (session) → end overlay (no title, no menus)\n865\t```\n866\t\n867\t| Scene | What it is |\n868\t|---|---|\n869\t| `title` | Night stadium under floodlights behind the logo; two Mudlarks passing a ball in the background (the real presentation, a tiny CPU loop); \"PRESS START\" (or the touch-only message); E.Arcade drives the idle cycle (`idle: 10`) |\n870\t| `menu` | BigMenu (scale 2): MEGA CUP (CONTINUE if a cup save exists), EXHIBITION, TRAINING GROUND, RECORDS, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS; a one-line description of the focused item; 10 s idle → attract |\n871\t| `attract` | the match scene with `{ attract: true }` (§13) |\n872\t| `cup` | the bracket: four big cards (ROUND ONE, QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, GRAND FINAL) with the opponent crest, venue, result or NEXT or LOCKED; PLAY NEXT MATCH, TRAINING, TEAM SHEET (seven portraits with nickname and role; ✕ on one shows its five stat bars), BACK |\n873\t| `story` | runs one `E.Story` node on a staged set (clubhouse, pitch-side, tunnel, podium; §9.3), then `go(next)`; ✕ turns pages, △ skips the scene |\n874\t| `join` | \"PRESS START TO JOIN\" (pads) or 2 (keyboard right half); each seat moves left/right to HOME, AWAY or CPU; in the cup only HOME; ✕ ready; up to 4 |\n875\t| `setup` | Exhibition: HOME and AWAY team cards (left/right to change; crest, name, three bars: SPEED, POWER, SKILL), VENUE (picture card), WEATHER (Venue default / Clear / Rain / Wind / Storm), TIME (Day / Dusk / Night), HALVES (2-5 min), SUDDEN DEATH (On/Off); PLAY |\n876\t| `match` | the match (pausable); data `{ home, away, venue, weather, time, half, cup, drill, attract, session, seed }` |\n877\t| `results` | the score with crests, PLAYER OF THE MATCH (portrait, two stats), four stat tiles, CONTINUE; a record set → initials (E.Arcade letter wheel) |\n878\t| `training` | the nine drills as big cards with a tick when done; ✕ plays one |\n879\t| `records` | three tables, one a page: BIGGEST WINS (margin), MOST TRIES IN A MATCH, BIGGEST HIT (metres flown); initials |\n880\t| `about` | five pages (§20); L1/R1 or left/right turns them |\n881\t| `credits` | rolls over the third half (§9.3), then the title |\n882\t| `card` | the AI Hub card (§15.2) |\n883\t\n884\t**Deep links** (for `tools/check.mjs`, filmstrips and screenshots, read from `location.hash` at start as the kits do):\n885\t`#title`, `#menu`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#training/<n>`, `#match` (an Exhibition with the defaults), `#match/<venue>`,\n886\t`#attract`, `#records`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#card` (the session card with made-up players, for screenshots only).\n887\t\n888\t**Pause menu** (standard, adjusted): Resume, RESTART MATCH, DEV MODE, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title\n889\t(none of these in a session, §15.2).\n890\t\n891\t**Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: false }` (no manual save slots: arcade); the cup autosaves at the cup hub\n892\tand after each match: `{ round, results: [[home, away]], seeds, difficulty, stats }` with `place: 'MEGA CUP'`, `level:\n893\tround`. CONTINUE on the menu loads `game.saves.latest()`. Records and unlocks in `E.store` (`thugby:records`,\n894\t`thugby:unlocks`). Winning the cup unlocks the MEGACORP MAULERS in Exhibition and a BIG HEADS cheat (Settings, Game).\n895\t\n896\t---\n897\t\n898\t## 9. Content\n899\t\n900\t### 9.1 Teams and rosters\n901\t\n902\tKit colours map to Humanoid `colors`: `cloth` jersey, `trim` collar and cuffs, `pants` shorts, `boot` boots, `belt`\n903\tthe shorts' band (trim colour). Headgear: `hat: { style: 'helmet', color }` is a scrum cap, `'band'` a headband. If two\n904\tteams' home jerseys differ in luminance by less than 60, the away team wears its away kit.\n905\t\n906\t**MUDDINGTON MUDLARKS** (the player's team; pub side from the Muddy Duck). Home: sky blue `#4aa0e0`, trim mud brown\n907\t`#5a3a1e`, shorts `#3a2a1a`, boots `#1a1410`. Away: cream `#e8dcc0`, trim `#4aa0e0`. Crest: a brown mudlark on a blue\n908\tshield. Style: balanced (aggression .5, pass .55, kick .3, cheap shots .1).\n909\t\n910\t| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n911\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n912\t| 1 | Dougie \"The Fridge\" McAllister (captain) | Prop | bulky 1.35 | bald, pale skin, scrum cap brown | 4 9 5 3 8 |\n913\t| 2 | Kev \"Gravy\" Boatwright | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | short ginger, headband | 5 8 6 3 7 |\n914\t| 3 | Sione \"Tiny\" Taufa | Prop | bulky 1.42 | short black, brown skin | 4 10 4 2 8 |\n915\t| 4 | Priya \"Pocket Rocket\" Nandakumar | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | ponytail black, brown skin | 8 4 9 6 6 |\n916\t| 5 | Ffion \"Boots\" Pritchard | Fly-half | heroic 1.12 | long auburn, pale | 6 5 8 9 5 |\n917\t| 6 | Marcus \"The Bus\" Odhiambo | Centre | heroic 1.30 | spiky black, dark skin | 7 8 6 4 7 |\n918\t| 7 | Jamie \"Wheels\" Whitlock | Wing | heroic 1.10 | spiky blond, pale | 10 4 7 5 4 |\n919\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b392508-0a9c-4851-a1e8-b9fce2e4b886","uuid":"133fd1c7-ff58-4560-bade-8fe6eafaa6a1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:56:34.785Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","content":"```\nintro → kickoff → play ⇄ (tackle → ruck → play)\n                       ⇄ (knockOn | forwardPass → scrum → play)\n                       ⇄ (touch → lineout → play)\n                       ⇄ (foul → [advantage] → penalty → choice → setKick | tapGo | kickToTouch→lineout)\n                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\nhooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n```\n\n- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n\n### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n\n- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n    ground.\n  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n    seat colour.\n\n### 7.3 The ball\n\n- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) updated with the map, so it bounces off the stands'\n  walls as the sports kit's ball does off its boards (on the field there are no walls: out of play is decided by the\n  lines, below); air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s; wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne.\n- **The oval bounce** (the soul of loose-ball chaos): on each ground contact with vertical speed above 30, rotate its\n  ground velocity by `±U(0, 70°) × bounceChaos` and scale its rebound height by `U(0.3, 1.25)`; a grubber bounces\n  higher at random (\"sat up nicely\"); all from `TT.rng`. Spin (end over end for kicks, spiral for passes) is drawn from\n  `ball.rot`.\n- Out of play: the ball's centre crossing a touchline (or the carrier's feet touching one) is **touch** → lineout to the\n  team that did not touch it last, at the x where it crossed (moved 51 u from the try lines). Crossing a dead-ball line\n  or touch-in-goal: if the attackers put it there → **22 drop-out** to the defenders; if the defenders did and it was\n  not a kick from in-goal → 5 m scrum to the attackers.\n- Pick-up: a loose ball below z 9 within 9 u of a player whose state accepts it (and 4.5 u if it moves faster than\n  210) is gathered; at full sprint 15% are fumbled forward (a knock-on) unless HND ≥ 8.\n\n### 7.4 Passing\n\n- **Who receives:** legal receivers are teammates not in front of the passer (`(rx - px) × dir ≤ 4`), within 220 u,\n  standing and not binned. L1 picks among those above the passer (smaller y), R1 among those below. Tap: the nearest by\n  `|dy|` within 110 u (short pass). Hold more than 0.25 s: the second-nearest on that side, or the nearest if he is the\n  only one (long pass, 300 u/s).\n- **Flight:** aim at the receiver's lead point `rx + rvx × t × 0.9` (t from distance / speed), launched with\n  `E.arc(..., { apex: 6 })` for short, `apex: 10` long; 230 u/s short.\n- **Catch:** in the receiver's 10 u reach and below z 30: chance = `catchBase × (0.9 + 0.01 × HND)`, minus 0.06 for a\n  long pass, minus `pressurePenalty` (0.12) with a defender within 20 u, minus 0.06 in rain; Grease Jersey and Iron\n  Shoulders do not change it; a pass from or to a player ON FIRE is always caught. A miss either drops forward\n  (knock-on) or spills loose (50/50 by the ball's direction).\n- **Forward pass:** judged as the law does, relative to the passer: if `(ball velocity - passer velocity) · dir > 4\n  u/s` at release, it is forward. The referee always calls it (whistle when caught or grounded): scrum to the other\n  team. Only a mouse click on a man in front (or no assist) can throw one; the hover shows it red first.\n- **Dummy:** a pass button with no legal receiver on that side (and pass assist off, or nobody anywhere) is a dummy:\n  the carrier sells it; each defender within 40 u with eyes on the carrier \"buys it\" with 40% (turns toward the fake\n  receiver for 0.3 s); +4 hype per defender sold.\n- **Offload:** within the first 0.15 s of being tackled (not a big hit), L1/R1 pops a short pass to a legal receiver\n  within 50 u; catch chance -0.1; +6 hype.\n- **Interception:** a pass that flies within 10 u of an opponent below z 24 can be taken: the CPU tries with\n  `0.15 × interceptMult`; a human holding ✕ near the lane (within 12 u) tries with 0.45. Success: the ball and +12 hype,\n  and usually a long run.\n\n### 7.5 Running moves\n\n- **Sidestep (✕ with the ball):** an impulse of `sidestepPower` (140 u/s) perpendicular to the run toward the stick's\n  side (no stick: away from the nearest defender), for `sidestepEvade` (0.25 s) any tackle attempt whiffs; cooldown\n  0.6 s. A whiffed tackler stumbles (0.5 s). +6 hype when it beats a committed tackler.\n- **Spin (✕ twice within 0.25 s):** 0.4 s evade, a full 360° body spin, 15% speed loss after; beats big hits too.\n- **Fend (□ with the ball):** opens a 0.3 s `fendWindow` (the stiff arm out). A standard tackle arriving inside it\n  fails with `fendBeat` (0.7) + 0.03 × (carrier POW - tackler TKL); a big hit fails with half that. A beaten tackler\n  is shoved back 20 u and sits down (0.8 s). Cooldown 0.8 s. +6 hype.\n- **Line break:** the carrier gets past the defensive line (every opponent but at most one, the deep sweeper, is now\n  behind him, nearer his own try line): banner \"LINE BREAK!\", +8 hype, support runners turbo.\n- **Grounding a try:** in the in-goal, ✕ dives and grounds (with style: +3 hype); otherwise the ball is grounded by\n  itself after 2.5 s in the in-goal, when within 16 u of the dead-ball line, or when tackled there (always a try,\n  arcade law). Running toward the posts before grounding makes the conversion easier: a real decision with the clock\n  and the chasers.\n\n### 7.6 Kicking\n\n- **Grubber (tap ○):** along the ground 140-200 u ahead (stick aims within ±45°), `vz` 40, extra bounce chaos.\n- **Punt (hold ○, release):** the meter fills in 0.9 s; while it fills the carrier runs straight on and the stick only\n  aims. Distance `lerp(120, kickMax (520), power) × (0.75 + 0.03 × KCK)`; apex 60-110; aimed by the stick (forward\n  cone ±70°; no stick: straight). Over 0.9 of the meter is the \"sweet spot\": +8% distance and true flight; outside, a\n  random hook of up to ±(11 - KCK)°.\n- **Bomb / up-and-under (punt with the stick pulled back at release):** apex 150, distance × 0.5; it hangs, and chasers\n  can contest the catch (§7.11).\n- **Kick to touch:** any punt aimed across a touchline goes out where it crosses: lineout to the other team (or to the\n  kicking team from a penalty, §7.12).\n- **Drop goal (hold ○ inside the opponents' 22, or within 300 u of their posts and facing them):** aimed at the posts\n  (the stick nudges it ±8°); power and accuracy as a punt; good if it passes between the uprights above the crossbar:\n  3 points. In that zone the stick pulled back at release still gives a bomb, and the stick pushed toward a touchline\n  a cross-field punt; otherwise a held kick is the drop goal (the prompt says so: \"{b:ci} HOLD: DROP GOAL\").\n- **Mouse:** right button hold and release kicks toward the cursor; the landing ring is drawn where it will come down at\n  the current fill; the kind follows the same rules (in their 22 facing the posts: a drop goal).\n- A landing marker (a pulsing ring decal) shows where every kick will come down, for both teams.\n\n### 7.7 Tackling\n\n- **Tackle (tap ✕ without the ball):** reaches 14 u (`tackleRange`) in front (within ±70° of facing). Chance =\n  `tackleBase (0.78) × (0.9 + 0.02 × TKL - 0.02 × carrier POW)`, plus 0.1 from the side or behind, plus the\n  difficulty bonus, minus 0.05 if the carrier is on turbo. Success: the paired `tackle` action (§11.2), then a ruck. Failure: \"broken\n  tackle\": the tackler falls (0.6 s), the carrier staggers 0.4 s and goes on (+5 hype to the attack).\n- **Big hit (hold ✕, let go in range):** charging takes `bigHitCharge` (0.7 s) to full; the charger moves at 1.15x and\n  glows. Let go within 18 u: chance `0.7 + 0.2 × charge`. Full charge = **MONSTER HIT**: the carrier is launched\n  (`bigHitLaunch`: 30-60 u back, z 20-40, a full flip), lands heavily and slides; the ball pops loose with\n  `spillChance` (0.5), forward = knock-on; hit-stop 0.12 s, flash, shake 6, rumble, the crowd \"OOOOH\", a replay. Held\n  past 1.2 s the charge goes red: a frontal hit then is a **high shot** (a foul, a yellow card if seen). A missed big\n  hit sprawls the hitter for 1.0 s.\n- **Dive tackle (□ without the ball):** a 0.35 s lunge of 30 u (`diveRange`); contact trips the carrier (an ankle tap:\n  he falls forward, a tackle); a miss leaves the diver down for 1.2 s.\n- **Gang tackle:** players with `immovable` (the boss, BIG UNIT; anyone in THUNDER RUN is simply unstoppable) are only\n  \"held\" by the first successful tackle (they slow to 40% and drag the tackler); a second tackle within 1.0 s brings\n  them down; otherwise they shrug it off after 1.2 s and the tackler is flung aside.\n- **Cheap shot:** ✕ on an opponent without the ball (within 14 u) is a shoulder barge: the victim is flattened for\n  1.6 s. It is a foul only if the referee sees it (§7.13). Unseen: +8 hype and Barry: \"The ref's missed that completely!\"\n- **Collisions:** launched bodies hitting other players knock them down (1.0 s); hitting the referee is REF DOWN.\n\n### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n\n- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.2 + 0.1 ×\n  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players. Mashing: a\n  side with a human seat (its controlled player committed, or the tackled carrier) is driven by that seat's presses of\n  ✕, each worth `mashWeight` (0.05), several humans adding up; a side with no human presses at `cpuMash` per second (±\n  20%). Worked example, two attackers (POW 8 + 6) against one defender (POW 8): the commitment adds +0.12 a second, so a\n  human who does not mash against a CPU at 9 presses a second ends at 0.3 + (0.12 - 0.45) × 1.6 = -0.23 (turnover); one\n  mashing at 12 against a CPU at 6 ends at +0.97.\n- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n  foul if seen.\n- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n  draws the line.\n\n### 7.9 Scrum\n\n- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n  (5 points, grounded at the scrum's y, so converted from in line with it).\n\n### 7.10 Lineout\n\n- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n  couch play).\n- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n  chose another pod, the throwers win it. If they chose the same pod, their jumper contests: attack score = 0.6 ×\n  throw quality (0-1, from the needle) + 0.04 × jumper HND + 0.15; defence score = 0.6 × timing (1 - |press - arrival|\n  / 0.3, clamped 0-1, from ✕ pressed as the ball arrives) + 0.04 × jumper HND; the higher score takes it (\"STOLEN!\").\n  The winner taps it down to his scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three\n  times running); a CPU defence picks the right pod with its difficulty's read chance, and its timing error is drawn\n  from its scrum timing σ.\n\n### 7.11 Kick-offs and 22 drop-outs\n\n- Kick-off from the centre spot by the fly-half (drop kick). The kicker aims a reticle (stick or mouse) on the\n  receiving half and holds ○ (or the left mouse button) for power, letting go to kick. It must travel 102 u (\"10 m\"):\n  short = \"NOT TEN!\" → a free kick to the receivers at halfway; straight into touch = a scrum to the receivers at\n  halfway.\n- Receivers catch automatically when the ball comes to a player in reach (10 u, z < 30). When a chaser and a receiver\n  both reach a high ball, it's a **contest**: each presses ✕ as it arrives; the better timing (CPU: by difficulty and\n  HND) takes it, the other is bumped down.\n- 22 drop-out: the same, by the defending team from its own 22 line, distance unlimited.\n\n### 7.12 Tries, conversions, penalties, free kicks\n\n- **Try:** 5 points; celebration (each player has a celebration, §11.2), then a replay if earned (§7.20), then the\n  conversion.\n- **Conversion** (and **penalty goal**) set kick, in the behind-the-kicker camera:\n  1. **Place:** move the tee back along the line through the grounding point parallel to touch (stick up/down, mouse\n     drag or wheel), 51-400 u from the try line; the angle and the distance read out (\"38 M\").\n  2. **Aim:** a reticle on the posts' plane, moved by the stick or the mouse; it sways a little (more for low KCK and\n     higher difficulty); a windsock and arrow show the wind.\n  3. **Power:** hold ○ (or the left mouse button) and let go: a meter needs to reach the distance's mark (shown); a\n     tight accuracy band near the top adds no hook; elsewhere hooks up to ±(12 - KCK)°.\n  4. **Flight:** the ball flies in 3D with the wind; it scores if it crosses the try line's plane between the uprights\n     above the crossbar; hitting an upright is a DOINK (it bounces off, missed).\n  A 20 s shot clock runs (the crowd's slow hand-clap speeds up). Conversion 2, penalty goal 3. CPU kicks are the same\n  flight with an error drawn from its kicker's stats.\n- **Penalty:** after a seen foul (and no advantage gained) the non-offending team's captain chooses on a big three-card\n  screen (stick or mouse; CPU chooses by score, time and distance): **TAP & GO** (play restarts at once; the offenders\n  are put 102 u back), **KICK AT GOAL** (if within 400 u; a set kick for 3), **KICK FOR TOUCH** (a punt aimed at the\n  touchline; the kicking team throws in at the lineout).\n- **Free kick** (early engagement, not ten): as a penalty, but no kick at goal.\n- **Penalty try:** a seen foul against a carrier within 60 u of the try line with no defender between him and the line:\n  7 points, no conversion.\n\n### 7.13 The referee and the laws he calls\n\n- **Referee Nigel Blewitt** is a Humanoid on the pitch (black kit, whistle). He runs to a spot 50 u behind the ball on\n  the attacking side and 40 u toward the far touchline (so he never stands between play and the camera), at 95 u/s,\n  steering round players; he turns to face the ball at 4 rad/s. His eyes: `E.sees(ref, offender, { range: refRange\n  (260), fov: refFov (1.4) })` at the moment of the foul and again 0.3 s later. A \"Show the ref's view\" setting (default\n  on) draws his `r.sightCone` faintly on the grass: the over-the-top tactic of fouling behind his back is part of the\n  game.\n- Always called (they are not about being seen): forward pass, knock-on, touch, not straight, early engagement, use it.\n- Called only if seen: **high shot** (an over-charged frontal big hit): penalty + yellow card; **cheap shot** (a hit on\n  a player without the ball): penalty, a yellow card for the same player's second; **offside** (a defender ahead of his\n  offside line closing on the ball within 30 u when it comes out of a ruck, scrum or lineout): penalty; **hands in the\n  ruck**: penalty.\n- **Advantage:** a seen foul by team A while team B has the ball or a loose ball near it: the referee calls ADVANTAGE B\n  (arm out) and play goes on; if B gains 100 u or scores within 5 s, ADVANTAGE OVER; if B loses the ball or 5 s pass\n  without gain, play comes back for the penalty at the mark.\n- **Cards and the sin bin:** a yellow card sends the player to the sin bin (the dumpster on the touchline) for `sinBin`\n  (30 s of running clock); his team plays with six; the AI shape adapts. A second yellow for the same player is a red\n  card: off for the match. A banner, the ref's card held high, the crowd boos, and a sad trombone.\n- **Ref down:** a launched body, the chicken or a flying bystander hitting the referee floors him for 8 s: no fouls are\n  called at all (cards, offside, cheap shots all free), \"REF DOWN! ANYTHING GOES!\", then he gets up and play goes on.\n- The referee's calls appear as speech balloons over him (\"CROUCH!\", \"BIND!\", \"SET!\", \"USE IT!\", \"ADVANTAGE!\", \"PLAY\n  ON!\", \"HANDS AWAY!\", \"PENALTY!\", \"KNOCK ON!\", \"FORWARD!\", \"NOT STRAIGHT!\") with his babble voice and arm signals.\n\n### 7.14 Scoring\n\n| Score | Points |\n|---|---|\n| Try (and pushover try) | 5 |\n| Conversion | 2 |\n| Penalty goal | 3 |\n| Drop goal | 3 |\n| Penalty try | 7 |\n\n### 7.15 Hype and supers\n\n- A HYPE meter per team (0-100), shown on the score bug. Gains (× `hypeMult`): tackle 4, broken tackle 5, sidestep or\n  fend that beats a man 6, dummy 4 per man sold, offload 6, line break 8, big hit 10, monster hit 16, interception 12,\n  jackal or ruck turnover 8, scrum won 6, lineout steal 8, try 15, conversion 5, drop goal 10, unseen cheap shot 8, air\n  horn 40.\n- Full: \"△ SUPER!\" flashes on the meter and over the team's controlled players.\n- **THUNDER RUN** (△ with the ball): `superTime` (4 s); the carrier is on fire, 1.35x speed, unstoppable (tacklers\n  bounce off and fly like skittles), the ball cannot be knocked loose; ends on a pass, a kick, a try or time.\n- **HURRICANE HIT** (△ without the ball): the controlled defender locks onto the carrier and homes in at 2x speed for\n  up to 2 s; contact is a guaranteed monster hit with the ball loose and everyone within 30 u knocked over; if the ball\n  is passed first, it re-targets the new carrier once.\n- CPU teams use supers: Thunder Run in the opponents' half with space ahead; Hurricane Hit when the opposing carrier is\n  within 120 u of their try line.\n\n### 7.16 ON FIRE\n\nA player who scores two tries in a row (no opposing score between) is ON FIRE until the other team scores or 90 s pass:\nunlimited turbo, passes and catches never fail, fends ×1.5, tackles on him ×0.6, kicks +20% distance, a flame trail\n(emissive), a music layer, \"HE'S ON FIRE!\".\n\n### 7.17 Power-ups (thrown on by the crowd)\n\nEvery `powerupEvery` (30 ± 10 s) of open play a fan in the stand throws one onto the pitch (an `E.arc` from the crowd\nto a spot at least 80 u from the ball); one at a time; it stays 15 s (blinking for the last 3). The first player to run\nover it takes it. The CPU diverts one off-ball player if it is within 100 u.\n\n| Power-up | Looks | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| MEAT PIE | a steaming pie in a foil tray | turbo refilled and unlimited for 6 s |\n| IRON SHOULDERS | riveted shoulder pads | 15 s: his tackles and fends always win; his hits are monster hits |\n| MEGA BOOT | a golden boot with wings | his team's next kick: ×1.6 distance, on fire; a set kick's accuracy band ×2 (60 s) |\n| GREASE JERSEY | a glistening jersey | 8 s: tackles on him fail 70% |\n| AIR HORN | a red air horn | +40 hype for his team at once; the crowd goes barmy |\n\n### 7.18 Venues: weather and hazards (one twist each; data in §9.2)\n\n| Venue | Weather | Hazard |\n|---|---|---|\n| Muddington Park | rain (0.7) | **mud** patches (4-6 floor-tag blobs): speed ×0.8, acceleration ×0.6, tackles +10%, ball skids; catches -6% in rain; kits get muddier as the match goes on (rig colours mixed toward brown by each player's time in mud and on the ground) |\n| Port Grumble Docks | gusty wind | **wind** that shifts every 15-25 s (strength 0-1, a windsock on the HUD) pushes airborne balls (40 u/s² × strength × `windMult`); **CAPTAIN CLUCKY**, the giant chicken mascot, invades every 50-70 s, runs across on an `E.Path` for about 6 s, bowling over everyone in his way (the carrier drops the ball), chased by the referee |\n| The Furnace | clear night | **flame jets**: grates 32 u inside each touchline (8 a side) erupt in sequences; each glows orange for 1.0 s (the warning), then burns for 1.2 s; anyone within 12 u is TOASTED (stunned 1.2 s, smoking, briefly blackened; a toasted carrier drops the ball); fireworks on every try |\n| The Megadome | thunderstorm (rain 0.9) | **lightning** every 20-30 s: a crackling ring (36 u) warns for 1.4 s at a spot 60-200 u from the ball, then a strike: a flash, thunder, a scorch decal; anyone inside is stunned 1.5 s (drawn as a skeleton for two frames: a shared `build: 'skeleton'` rig drawn in their place) and a carrier inside drops the ball |\n\n`hazardEvery` (×1.0) scales every hazard's frequency; 0 turns them off.\n\n### 7.19 AI\n\nBoth CPU teams and the CPU teammates of humans run the same brain; difficulty and the team's style (§9.1) change its\nnumbers, never its logic. Shapes are recomputed every 0.25 s per team (staggered); decisions every 0.15 s plus the\nreaction delay.\n\n- **Attack shape** (team in possession; carrier at `(cx, cy)`, attacking direction `d`): six support slots in a\n  staggered line behind the carrier, three each side: slot k at `(cx - d × (18 + 10k), cy ∓ 44k)` (spacing 44 to the\n  open side, 36 to the blind side), clamped 20 u inside touch. Forwards take the k = 1 slots, backs the wider ones, the\n  wing the widest open-side slot; then nearest-first; a reassignment needs a 20 u improvement (hysteresis). Supporters\n  never stand in front of the carrier (they check stride to stay 6 u behind). After a line break they turbo.\n- **Defence shape:** a line at `cx + d × 30` facing the attack (behind the offside line when there is one), defenders\n  paired to attackers by y order (\"man on man drift\") so the line slides with the attack; the nearest defender by\n  intercept time is the **tackler** (aims at the carrier's predicted position), the second the **cover** (20 u behind\n  and inside); the **sweeper** (the wing or fly-half) sits 140 u deep at `lerp(cy, CY, .5)` to field kicks, and joins\n  the line when the ball is within 200 u of his try line. With six men (sin bin) the line spaces wider.\n- **Tackler decisions:** in range and facing, after `aiReaction`: try with `0.6 + 0.3 × aggression`; a big hit if POW\n  ≥ 7 or aggression ≥ 0.6 and the carrier is coming head on (charging from 40 u out); a dive tackle when chasing a\n  faster carrier from 18-30 u behind; cheap shots on the nearest support runner when the referee is not looking, with\n  the team's `cheapShots` rate.\n- **Carrier decisions** (CPU carriers, and the human's teammates when they have the ball): score each option and take\n  the best, with noise by difficulty: run forward (space in a 30° cone ahead), pass to each legal receiver (his space\n  minus defenders near the lane), sidestep (a tackler committing within 22 u: 25% × skill), fend (a tackler within 16 u\n  and POW ≥ 6: 40%), kick (deep in his own 22 under pressure: to touch; behind a flat line with a fast chaser: grubber\n  or chip; the last 20 s, trailing by 3 or less, in range: drop goal), dive in the in-goal (or run to the posts when no\n  defender is within 60 u). Steer toward the widest gap in the defensive line; keep 20 u inside touch; turbo in space\n  and when racing to the line; keep 30% of the tank.\n- **Loose ball:** the two nearest from each team chase its predicted rest point; the rest keep their shape.\n- **Kicks:** the receiving team's nearest (or the sweeper) goes to the landing marker, a second supports; the kicking\n  team's two fastest chase. (There is no offside in open play in this game; this is deliberate.)\n- **Set pieces:** see each set piece above. CPU kick-offs aim short and contestable, 120-200 u past halfway toward a\n  touchline. CPU penalty choice: kick at goal within 300 u when the score is close or late; kick to touch from far; tap\n  & go within 50 u of the line or when trailing late.\n- **Difficulty** (the player's Settings choice shifts each cup opponent one step):\n\n| | Rookie | Pro | Legend |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `aiReaction` | 0.40 s | 0.25 s | 0.14 s |\n| Tackle chance | -0.12 | 0 | +0.08 |\n| `cpuMash` | 6/s | 9/s | 12/s |\n| Decision noise | 0.35 | 0.20 | 0.08 |\n| Interception × | 0.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n| Scrum timing σ | 0.25 s | 0.12 s | 0.06 s |\n| Early engagement | 8% | 3% | 0% |\n| Lineout read | 0.25 | 0.35 | 0.45 |\n\n### 7.20 Instant replay\n\n- A ring buffer keeps the `MatchState` of the last 5 s at 60 Hz (every other step).\n- Triggers: monster hits, supers, tries that came from a run of 200 u or more or beat a man, drop goals, pushover\n  tries, interception tries; at most one replay in 30 s (tries always). Setting: Replays Big moments (default) / All\n  tries / Off.\n- Playback: the window from 2.5 s before to 1 s after the event, at 0.5x, through the normal presentation (states fed\n  to the rigs), camera at zoom 1.35 on the key actor, letterbox bars, \"INSTANT REPLAY\" in the corner, Barry: \"Let's see\n  that again!\"; any button skips. After a try it plays in the celebration, before the conversion. Never in AI Hub\n  sessions.\n\n### 7.21 Stats and the Player of the Match\n\nPer team: possession % (time holding the ball), territory % (ball in the opponents' half), tries, conversions\nmade/attempted, penalties conceded, tackles made/missed, big hits, monster hits, metres carried (`units / 10.24`), line\nbreaks, turnovers won, offloads, cards. Player of the Match (winning side): tries × 10 + monster hits × 4 + tackles + metres\n/ 10 + line breaks × 3 + turnovers × 3. Results show four tiles: TRIES, BIG HITS, METRES, POSSESSION.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Modes, scenes and flow\n\n```\nboot → title ─(10 s idle)→ attract ─(any input)→ title\n         │ PRESS START\n         ▼\n       menu ─(10 s idle)→ attract\n         ├─ MEGA CUP ─→ cup hub ─→ story (prologue) → training (optional) → story (pre-match) → [join] → match\n         │                 ▲                                                                        │\n         │                 └──── results (win: next round; loss: CONTINUE? 10 s) ←───────────────────┘\n         │                 final won → story (trophy) → story (third half) → credits → title\n         ├─ EXHIBITION → join → setup (teams, venue, weather, time, halves) → match → results → rematch | menu\n         ├─ TRAINING GROUND → drill list → match (drill) → next drill | list\n         ├─ RECORDS → three tables (attract-style)\n         ├─ SETTINGS → the standard settings screen (game.menu('settings'))\n         └─ ABOUT & CREDITS → five pages\nAI Hub session: boot → card (the game's own) → match (session) → end overlay (no title, no menus)\n```\n\n| Scene | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `title` | Night stadium under floodlights behind the logo; two Mudlarks passing a ball in the background (the real presentation, a tiny CPU loop); \"PRESS START\" (or the touch-only message); E.Arcade drives the idle cycle (`idle: 10`) |\n| `menu` | BigMenu (scale 2): MEGA CUP (CONTINUE if a cup save exists), EXHIBITION, TRAINING GROUND, RECORDS, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS; a one-line description of the focused item; 10 s idle → attract |\n| `attract` | the match scene with `{ attract: true }` (§13) |\n| `cup` | the bracket: four big cards (ROUND ONE, QUARTER-FINAL, SEMI-FINAL, GRAND FINAL) with the opponent crest, venue, result or NEXT or LOCKED; PLAY NEXT MATCH, TRAINING, TEAM SHEET (seven portraits with nickname and role; ✕ on one shows its five stat bars), BACK |\n| `story` | runs one `E.Story` node on a staged set (clubhouse, pitch-side, tunnel, podium; §9.3), then `go(next)`; ✕ turns pages, △ skips the scene |\n| `join` | \"PRESS START TO JOIN\" (pads) or 2 (keyboard right half); each seat moves left/right to HOME, AWAY or CPU; in the cup only HOME; ✕ ready; up to 4 |\n| `setup` | Exhibition: HOME and AWAY team cards (left/right to change; crest, name, three bars: SPEED, POWER, SKILL), VENUE (picture card), WEATHER (Venue default / Clear / Rain / Wind / Storm), TIME (Day / Dusk / Night), HALVES (2-5 min), SUDDEN DEATH (On/Off); PLAY |\n| `match` | the match (pausable); data `{ home, away, venue, weather, time, half, cup, drill, attract, session, seed }` |\n| `results` | the score with crests, PLAYER OF THE MATCH (portrait, two stats), four stat tiles, CONTINUE; a record set → initials (E.Arcade letter wheel) |\n| `training` | the nine drills as big cards with a tick when done; ✕ plays one |\n| `records` | three tables, one a page: BIGGEST WINS (margin), MOST TRIES IN A MATCH, BIGGEST HIT (metres flown); initials |\n| `about` | five pages (§20); L1/R1 or left/right turns them |\n| `credits` | rolls over the third half (§9.3), then the title |\n| `card` | the AI Hub card (§15.2) |\n\n**Deep links** (for `tools/check.mjs`, filmstrips and screenshots, read from `location.hash` at start as the kits do):\n`#title`, `#menu`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#training/<n>`, `#match` (an Exhibition with the defaults), `#match/<venue>`,\n`#attract`, `#records`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#card` (the session card with made-up players, for screenshots only).\n\n**Pause menu** (standard, adjusted): Resume, RESTART MATCH, DEV MODE, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title\n(none of these in a session, §15.2).\n\n**Saves:** `game.saves` with `menu: { saves: false }` (no manual save slots: arcade); the cup autosaves at the cup hub\nand after each match: `{ round, results: [[home, away]], seeds, difficulty, stats }` with `place: 'MEGA CUP'`, `level:\nround`. CONTINUE on the menu loads `game.saves.latest()`. Records and unlocks in `E.store` (`thugby:records`,\n`thugby:unlocks`). Winning the cup unlocks the MEGACORP MAULERS in Exhibition and a BIG HEADS cheat (Settings, Game).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Content\n\n### 9.1 Teams and rosters\n\nKit colours map to Humanoid `colors`: `cloth` jersey, `trim` collar and cuffs, `pants` shorts, `boot` boots, `belt`\nthe shorts' band (trim colour). Headgear: `hat: { style: 'helmet', color }` is a scrum cap, `'band'` a headband. If two\nteams' home jerseys differ in luminance by less than 60, the away team wears its away kit.\n\n**MUDDINGTON MUDLARKS** (the player's team; pub side from the Muddy Duck). Home: sky blue `#4aa0e0`, trim mud brown\n`#5a3a1e`, shorts `#3a2a1a`, boots `#1a1410`. Away: cream `#e8dcc0`, trim `#4aa0e0`. Crest: a brown mudlark on a blue\nshield. Style: balanced (aggression .5, pass .55, kick .3, cheap shots .1).\n\n| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Dougie \"The Fridge\" McAllister (captain) | Prop | bulky 1.35 | bald, pale skin, scrum cap brown | 4 9 5 3 8 |\n| 2 | Kev \"Gravy\" Boatwright | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | short ginger, headband | 5 8 6 3 7 |\n| 3 | Sione \"Tiny\" Taufa | Prop | bulky 1.42 | short black, brown skin | 4 10 4 2 8 |\n| 4 | Priya \"Pocket Rocket\" Nandakumar | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | ponytail black, brown skin | 8 4 9 6 6 |\n| 5 | Ffion \"Boots\" Pritchard | Fly-half | heroic 1.12 | long auburn, pale | 6 5 8 9 5 |\n| 6 | Marcus \"The Bus\" Odhiambo | Centre | heroic 1.30 | spiky black, dark skin | 7 8 6 4 7 |\n| 7 | Jamie \"Wheels\" Whitlock | Wing | heroic 1.10 | spiky blond, pale | 10 4 7 5 4 |\n","numLines":450,"startLine":470,"totalLines":1679}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MT2P86bbnRDv1NAsMkmp3j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1B4h2LTaRUTikqyfUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MKRsnchjxCqAi1JEf1owSW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":920,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14985,"cache_read_input_tokens":24515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14985},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b392508-0a9c-4851-a1e8-b9fce2e4b886","uuid":"788c54f4-964b-4935-b2ba-1d4051014817","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:56:35.519Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1B4NSGRYE8TMDBccAa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MKRsnchjxCqAi1JEf1owSW":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","offset":920,"limit":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MKRsnchjxCqAi1JEf1owSW","type":"tool_result","content":"920\tAlso: COACH GORDON GRISTLE (ex-prop, 60s: bulky 1.3, bald with grey fringe, flat cap `hat: 'cap'`, `outfit: 'coat'`\n921\tbrown), BIG DAVE (the bus driver: bulky 1.35, beanie-like `hat: 'band'`, hi-vis jacket `coat` `#e8e030`).\n922\t\n923\t**BRAMBLEWICK BADGERS** (round one; a village side). Home: black `#24242a`, trim white `#f0f0f0`, shorts white. Away:\n924\twhite, trim black, shorts black. Crest: a badger's striped face. Style: cautious (aggression .3, pass .4, kick .5,\n925\tcheap shots .05). Difficulty base: Rookie.\n926\t\n927\t| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n928\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n929\t| 1 | Edna \"Nan\" Pemberton (captain, 74) | Prop | bulky 1.25, `hunch: .2` | short grey hair, knitted scrum cap cream | 3 8 6 4 8 |\n930\t| 2 | Barnaby \"Barn Door\" Pike | Prop | bulky 1.38 | bald, ruddy | 3 9 3 2 7 |\n931\t| 3 | Wilf Hollins | Hooker | bulky 1.2 | short brown | 4 7 5 3 6 |\n932\t| 4 | Pip Tanner | Scrum-half | heroic 1.0 | spiky ginger | 7 3 7 5 5 |\n933\t| 5 | Clementine Ashby | Fly-half | heroic 1.1 | ponytail blonde | 5 4 7 8 4 |\n934\t| 6 | Ollie \"Badger\" Brock | Centre | heroic 1.25 | short black, grey streak | 6 7 5 3 6 |\n935\t| 7 | Tilly Fenwick | Wing | heroic 1.08 | long black | 8 3 6 4 4 |\n936\t\n937\t**PORT GRUMBLE GULLS** (quarter-final; a flashy harbour side). Home: white `#f4f4f0`, trim teal `#1fa89a`, shorts navy\n938\t`#1e2a50`. Away: teal, trim white, navy. Crest: a gull with a chip. Style: running and kicking (aggression .45, pass\n939\t.75, kick .5, cheap shots .1). Difficulty base: Pro, reaction 0.3 s. Mascot: CAPTAIN CLUCKY.\n940\t\n941\t| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n942\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n943\t| 1 | Sal \"Salty\" Pereira | Prop | bulky 1.32 | short black | 4 8 5 3 7 |\n944\t| 2 | Kenji \"Kipper\" Ito | Hooker | bulky 1.2 | spiky black | 6 7 7 3 6 |\n945\t| 3 | Mo \"Anchor\" Haddad | Prop | bulky 1.38 | bald | 4 9 4 2 8 |\n946\t| 4 | Lulu Fairweather | Scrum-half | heroic 1.02 | ponytail red | 8 4 9 6 5 |\n947\t| 5 | Jonty \"Silky\" Swift (captain) | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | long golden, a headband | 7 5 9 9 4 |\n948\t| 6 | Dexter \"Jet\" Okoro | Centre | heroic 1.25 | short, dark skin | 8 7 7 4 6 |\n949\t| 7 | Bree \"Breeze\" Lindqvist | Wing | heroic 1.1 | long platinum | 10 4 8 5 4 |\n950\t\n951\t**FURNACE FORGE IRONSIDES** (semi-final; foundry hard men and women). Home: charcoal `#3a3a44`, trim molten orange\n952\t`#f07a1e`, shorts black. Away: orange, trim charcoal. Crest: an anvil in flames. Style: big hitters (aggression .85,\n953\tpass .35, kick .25, cheap shots .35, line speed fast). Difficulty base: Pro. Most wear scrum caps in orange.\n954\t\n955\t| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n956\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n957\t| 1 | Grigor \"The Kiln\" Petrov | Prop | bulky 1.4 | bald, a soot smudge (skin darker) | 4 10 3 2 9 |\n958\t| 2 | \"Rusty\" Nailor | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | short rust-red | 5 8 5 3 8 |\n959\t| 3 | Bertha \"Big Bertha\" Blunt | Prop | bulky 1.4 | ponytail black | 4 10 4 2 9 |\n960\t| 4 | Smudge Cole | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | spiky black | 7 5 7 5 6 |\n961\t| 5 | Ingot Ingram | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | short blond | 6 6 7 8 6 |\n962\t| 6 | Adaeze \"Anvil\" Okafor (captain) | Centre | bulky 1.32 | short black, dark skin | 7 9 6 3 9 |\n963\t| 7 | Flint Mackay | Wing | heroic 1.12 | spiky grey | 9 6 6 4 6 |\n964\t\n965\t**MEGACORP MAULERS** (the grand final; a billionaire's bought-in super team; unlocked after the cup). Home: gold\n966\t`#e8c040`, trim purple `#5a2a8a`, shorts `#3a1a5a`. Away: purple, trim gold. Crest: a gold \"M\" in a purple diamond.\n967\tStyle: everything (aggression .7, pass .6, kick .45, cheap shots .25, supers eagerly). Difficulty base: Legend. Owner:\n968\tSIR RUPERT GOLDBRICK (cutscenes only: heroic 1.15, `outfit: 'coat'` purple, `hat: 'crown'` gold, a monocle drawn as one\n969\tpixel ring).\n970\t\n971\t| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n972\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n973\t| 1 | \"BIG UNIT\" Brannigan (captain, the boss) | Prop | bulky **2.0** | bald, a gold headband | 6 12 6 3 10 (POW beyond the scale on purpose) |\n974\t| 2 | Leverage Lou | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | slicked short | 6 8 7 3 7 |\n975\t| 3 | \"Bonus\" Barrington | Prop | bulky 1.38 | short blond | 5 9 5 2 8 |\n976\t| 4 | Synergy Jones | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | ponytail violet | 9 5 9 6 6 |\n977\t| 5 | Chad Sterling III | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | long gold, smug | 7 6 9 10 5 |\n978\t| 6 | Vance Capitale | Centre | heroic 1.28 | spiky black | 8 8 7 5 7 |\n979\t| 7 | Hedge Fundsworth | Wing | heroic 1.12 | short silver | 10 5 8 6 5 |\n980\t\n981\tBIG UNIT is `immovable` (gang tackle needed), his fend flings tacklers 40 u, all his tackles are big hits, and his\n982\tsuper is the UNIT TRAIN (a 6 s Thunder Run). He gets a spotlight entrance.\n983\t\n984\tCommentators and referee (portraits only, plus the referee on the pitch): BARRY BELLOWS (heroic 1.1, comb-over, a\n985\tblazer `coat` maroon, headset drawn as a dark band), ROS RUCKER (heroic 1.1, short grey bob, cauliflower ear: a pink\n986\tpixel blob; blazer navy), NIGEL BLEWITT (heroic 1.1, black kit with green trim, short brown hair, big ears).\n987\t\n988\t### 9.2 Venues (data: `{ id, name, time, weather, wind, lights, grass, stands, crowd, boards, skyline, hazard, music }`)\n989\t\n990\t| Venue | Look | Skyline beyond the far stand | Boards (fictional sponsors) | Music |\n991\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n992\t| **Muddington Park** (Mudlarks' home; the training ground too, by day without rain) | overcast day; a small wooden stand (`face: 'plank'`) and grass banks; the Muddy Duck pub behind the east in-goal | low hills, a church spire, drizzle | THE MUDDY DUCK · PIES & PINTS, BIG DAVE'S BUSES, CHANNEL THUD | \"Mud and Glory\" |\n993\t| **Port Grumble Docks** | dusk, orange sky; a concrete stand; shipping containers stacked behind one end | cranes, a lighthouse, gulls wheeling | SEAGULL-PROOF CHIPS, KRAKEN INSURANCE, GRUMBLE'S GRAVY | \"Grumble Shanty\" |\n994\t| **The Furnace** | night, floodlights (4 towers); black steel stands (`face: 'stone'` dark); glowing grates | chimneys belching sparks, a red glow | FORGEWORKS STEEL, TURBO TONIC, MEGA MEAT PIES | \"Forge Floor\" |\n995\t| **The Megadome** | night storm; a huge gold and purple bowl, a jumbotron on the far stand, lasers on tries | city towers, a GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS sign | GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS, CHANNEL THUD, TURBO TONIC | \"Megadome Mayhem\" |\n996\t\n997\tLighting (every scene is lit, as the look target asks): day `lights.enabled = true` with ambient 0.95 and a warm tint;\n998\tdusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool under each tower, `lights.add` every\n999\tdraw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames. Crowd: stand tiles hold two figures\n1000\teach (as the sports kit) in the two teams' colours (home 70%), bobbing; they jump on scores and boo cards; a Mexican wave\n1001\trolls round when play is stopped longer than 8 s. Floodlight towers: tall lamp props or custom shapes on the stand\n1002\tcorners.\n1003\t\n1004\t### 9.3 The Mega Cup: story beats and script\n1005\t\n1006\tWrite all story text in this voice: broadcast hype, pub banter, clichés turned up to eleven. Lines are `E.Story` nodes\n1007\t(data in `03-data-content.js`), spoken with portraits and babble voices; ALL CAPS shouts shake (`{shake}`); pauses with\n1008\t`{w=.4}`. The lines below are the spine; add up to two more per scene in the same style, no more.\n1009\t\n1010\t1. **Prologue: the Muddy Duck** (clubhouse set: plank floor `E.tex.planks`, plaster walls, a bar of counters, barrels,\n1011\t   stools, a dartboard, a pie warmer glowing, warm lamps; threequarter view, zoom 1.5).\n1012\t   - BIG DAVE: \"So I'm filling in the form, right. 'Mega Cup.' I thought it was a tea thing.\"\n1013\t   - GRISTLE: \"It's the TURBO SEVENS MEGA CUP, Dave. Live on Channel Thud. Against teams with dieticians.\"\n1014\t   - THE FRIDGE: \"We've got a dietician.\" *(nods at the pie warmer)*\n1015\t   - GRISTLE: \"Gristle's Rule Number One: nobody laughs at the Mudlarks. Rule Number Two: we train. Now. Yes, you too,\n1016\t     Dave.\"\n1017\t   - Choice: TRAIN (→ training) / SKIP TO THE CUP.\n1018\t2. **Round one vs Bramblewick Badgers, Muddington Park** (pitch-side set: the two captains face to face at halfway,\n1019\t   zoom 1.4).\n1020\t   - BARRY: \"Welcome to a damp Muddington Park, where the Mudlarks open their Mega Cup against the Bramblewick Badgers!\"\n1021\t   - ROS: \"Damp is generous, Barry. I've seen drier rivers.\"\n1022\t   - NAN PEMBERTON: \"I've propped since before your dad had teeth, sonny. I've had hip replacements tougher than you.\"\n1023\t   - GRISTLE: \"She's seventy-four, lads. Do NOT go easy on her. She bites.\"\n1024\t   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"Rule Three: hold the ball. Rule Four: see Rule Three.\"\n1025\t   - Won: BARRY: \"The Mudlarks are through! Ros, are they any good?\" ROS: \"They're... present, Barry.\"\n1026\t3. **Quarter-final vs Port Grumble Gulls, Port Grumble Docks.**\n1027\t   - JONTY SWIFT: \"Gorgeous evening. Gorgeous ground. Gorgeous me. Do try to keep up, darlings.\"\n1028\t   - GRISTLE: \"Watch the wind. Watch the chicken. Don't ask about the chicken.\"\n1029\t   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"Pass it like it's hot. It IS hot. It's Port Grumble. Everything here's been deep-fried.\"\n1030\t   - Won: ROS: \"That chicken has more caps than I do.\"\n1031\t4. **Semi-final vs Furnace Forge Ironsides, The Furnace.**\n1032\t   - ANVIL OKAFOR: \"We forge champions here. Everyone else, we melt down for scrap.\"\n1033\t   - GRISTLE: \"Don't stand on the glowing bits. Wheels. Wheels, look at me. The GLOWING bits.\"\n1034\t   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"They hit hard? Hit harder. Then hide behind Tiny.\"\n1035\t   - Won: BARRY: \"A PUB TEAM IN THE MEGA CUP FINAL! Somebody pinch me!\" ROS: \"Gladly, Barry.\"\n1036\t5. **Grand final vs Megacorp Maulers, The Megadome** (tunnel set; lights down, a spotlight for BIG UNIT).\n1037\t   - SIR RUPERT GOLDBRICK: \"Charming little pub team. I'll buy the lot of you. The pub, the pies, the muddy bird. Name\n1038\t     your price.\"\n1039\t   - THE FRIDGE: \"Not for sale.\"\n1040\t   - GRISTLE: \"The pies are for sale. Two-fifty. WE'RE not.\"\n1041\t   - BIG UNIT: \"*(one long babble roar)*\" BARRY: \"BIG UNIT BRANNIGAN! Two metres of pure invoice!\" ROS: \"You'll need two\n1042\t     men to bring him down, minimum. Bring a ladder.\"\n1043\t   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"I've written the big speech. In my head. It's very moving. Pretend I said it. NOW GET OUT\n1044\t     THERE!\"\n1045\t6. **Victory** (podium set: confetti, fireworks, the MEGA CUP trophy, a gaudy golden cup twice a man's height).\n1046\t   - BARRY: \"THE MUDDINGTON MUDLARKS ARE MEGA CUP CHAMPIONS! A PUB TEAM, ROS! A PUB TEAM!\"\n1047\t   - ROS: \"I need a lie down, Barry.\"\n1048\t   - SIR RUPERT: \"I'll buy the trophy, then.\" GRISTLE: \"Rule Five: no.\"\n1049\t7. **The third half** (back at the Muddy Duck; everyone cheering, Nan Pemberton and Captain Clucky included; the cast\n1050\t   sings the club song in a babble choir with lyrics on screen):\n1051\t   *\"Oh Muddington, oh Muddington, your mud is in my soul / We lost our boots, we lost our teeth, we never lost the\n1052\t   ball...\"* GRISTLE: \"Last orders!\" → credits.\n1053\t- **A lost match:** GRISTLE: \"Rule Six: we go again.\" → E.Arcade `continue(10)`: CONTINUE? (✕ retries the match with a\n1054\t  new seed; at zero, back to the cup hub with the match still NEXT).\n1055\t\n1056\tDrawn-out cutscenes are skippable (△); a skipped scene never blocks progress.\n1057\t\n1058\t### 9.4 Training Ground (Coach Gristle's drills)\n1059\t\n1060\tEach drill is a match scene with a scripted setup, a goal predicate, a prompt line with glyphs, and a **SHOW ME** (△)\n1061\tbutton where the coach's AI does it once (\"Watch me, you muppets\"). Its `auto` script is the same one the tests use to\n1062\tprove it can be completed. ○ / Esc leaves; a failed attempt resets in 1 s.\n1063\t\n1064\t| # | Drill | Setup | Goal | Teaches |\n1065\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1066\t| 1 | LEGS | you with the ball at your 22, cones to the try line | run to the line on turbo, dive (✕) over | moving, turbo, grounding |\n1067\t| 2 | HANDS | you and four runners in a line | five passes, both directions, then a long pass; a forward pass to Wheels shows the whistle | L1/R1, long pass, the backwards rule |\n1068\t| 3 | FEET | three tackle bags and a defender | sidestep twice, spin once, fend the defender | ✕ sidestep and spin, □ fend |\n1069\t| 4 | HIT | a runner coming at you, then another | a tackle, a BIG HIT (hold ✕), a dive tackle (□), switching (○ and L1/R1) | defence |\n1070\t| 5 | RUCK | three tackles in a row | win two rucks by mashing, then jackal one (□) | breakdown |\n1071\t| 6 | BOOT | you with the ball | a grubber into the in-goal and chase it; a punt into touch; a drop goal from 30 m | kicking |\n1072\t| 7 | SET PIECES | the forwards | win a scrum (✕ on SET, alternate L1/R1), win a lineout (call a pod, throw) | scrum, lineout |\n1073\t| 8 | POSTS | a try just scored out wide | convert it: place, aim, power | set kicks |\n1074\t| 9 | TURBO TIME | hype full, a meat pie on the pitch | take the pie, then THUNDER RUN through three defenders to score | power-ups, supers |\n1075\t\n1076\t### 9.5 Commentary\n1077\t\n1078\tThe director listens to the bus, picks a line by category with priorities (a try beats a pass), cooldowns (no category\n1079\ttwice in 6 s, no line twice in a match: shuffle bags), alternates Barry (play-by-play, first) and Ros (colour, a beat\n1080\tlater, 40% of the time), fills `{$player}` (nickname), `{$team}`, `{$score}`, `{$venue}`, and shows it on the radio\n1081\tdialog (`modal: false`, `auto: 2.2`, at the bottom, portraits). Setting: Commentary On / Text only / Off. Write at least\n1082\tsix lines per category in this voice:\n1083\t\n1084\t| Category | Lines (Barry unless marked Ros) |\n1085\t|---|---|\n1086\t| kick-off | \"And we're underway at {$venue}!\" · \"Big boot to get us going!\" · Ros: \"Here we go. Mind the mud.\" |\n1087\t| try | \"HE'S GONE OVER! TRY TIME!\" · \"Under the sticks! You could drive a bus through that gap!\" · \"Dotted down! {$player}, take a bow!\" · \"In at the corner! Somebody check the paint on that touchline!\" · Ros: \"Textbook. If the textbook was written by a hurricane.\" |\n1088\t| big hit | \"OH, THAT'S A BIG ONE!\" · \"He'll feel that in the morning. And the morning after.\" · \"Absolutely SHUDDERING!\" · Ros: \"I felt that in my old knee, Barry.\" |\n1089\t| monster hit | \"MONSTER HIT! That's gone into orbit!\" · \"Put him in Row Z!\" · \"Somebody get that man a postcode, he's lost!\" |\n1090\t| sidestep / spin | \"Left him for dead!\" · \"Feet like a ballroom dancer!\" · Ros: \"Lovely footwork. Questionable haircut. Lovely footwork.\" |\n1091\t| fend | \"HAND-OFF! Right in the chops!\" · \"He's fended him into next week!\" |\n1092\t| dummy | \"Oh, the dummy! They've bought it, the whole shop!\" |\n1093\t| line break | \"He's through! There's daylight!\" · \"The line's been cut like a birthday cake!\" |\n1094\t| knock-on | \"Knock-on. Butter fingers.\" · \"Dropped it like a hot pie!\" |\n1095\t| forward pass | \"Forward! The ref's not having that.\" · Ros: \"Forward by a country mile, Barry.\" |\n1096\t| ruck / jackal / turnover | \"JACKAL! He's pinched it!\" · \"Turnover! Stolen like a pie at a buffet!\" |\n1097\t| scrum | \"Crouch... bind... SET! And they've hit like freight trains!\" · Ros: \"That scrum's going backwards, and so is their dignity.\" |\n1098\t| pushover try | \"PUSHOVER TRY! They've shoved them over the line like a wardrobe!\" |\n1099\t| lineout | \"He's been lifted so high he can see his house!\" · \"Stolen at the lineout! Cheeky!\" |\n1100\t| conversion made / missed | \"Straight between the sticks!\" · \"Bang! Two more!\" · \"Wide! Hooked it like a fisherman.\" · \"DOINK! Off the upright!\" |\n1101\t| drop goal | \"DROP GOAL! Cheeky, cheeky!\" |\n1102\t| penalty / advantage | \"Penalty! The ref's arm is out!\" · \"Advantage being played...\" · \"Advantage over.\" |\n1103\t| unseen cheap shot | \"Ooh... the ref's missed that one completely.\" · \"What the ref doesn't see, Ros...\" Ros: \"...is still assault, Barry.\" |\n1104\t| yellow / red | \"YELLOW CARD! Off to the sin bin, and I mean an actual bin!\" · \"RED CARD! Early bath!\" |\n1105\t| ref down | \"THE REF'S DOWN! Anything goes, Barry!\" (Ros says it; Barry: \"Anything goes, Ros!\") |\n1106\t| on fire | \"HE'S ON FIRE!\" · \"Somebody call the fire brigade! Actually, don't, let it burn!\" |\n1107\t| super | \"THUNDER RUN! Get out of the way!\" · \"HURRICANE HIT INCOMING!\" |\n1108\t| power-up | \"Somebody's chucked a meat pie on the pitch!\" Ros: \"Is that... gravy?\" · \"IRON SHOULDERS! He's a walking wardrobe!\" · \"The MEGA BOOT! Stand well back!\" · \"Grease jersey! Slippery as a sardine!\" · \"AIR HORN! The crowd's gone barmy!\" |\n1109\t| hazards | \"It's CAPTAIN CLUCKY! The mascot's on the pitch again!\" · \"Mind the flames! That's a well-done winger!\" · \"Lightning strike! That's one way to clear a ruck!\" · \"He's in the mud! Half man, half puddle!\" |\n1110\t| hooter / half / full / sudden death | \"There's the hooter! Ball has to go dead!\" · \"Half-time here at {$venue}: {$score}.\" · \"FULL TIME! {$team} win it, {$score}!\" · \"That's it! Somebody get the kettle on!\" · \"Golden point! Next score wins the lot!\" |\n1111\t\n1112\t### 9.6 Records and unlocks\n1113\t\n1114\tE.Arcade tables (`id: 'thugby'`), modes `margin`, `tries`, `hit` (metres flown × 10), seeded with ten fictional\n1115\tentries each (initials of the cast: \"NAN 34\", \"BIG 12\"...). After an Exhibition or cup match, any qualifying number\n1116\topens the initials wheel. Unlocks as in §8.\n1117\t\n1118\t---\n1119\t\n1120\t## 10. Art direction and presentation\n1121\t\n1122\t### 10.1 The engine's look target, applied\n1123\t\n1124\t`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`; HD Humanoids at size 1.0-1.42 (the boss 2.0), every character dressed (outfit `shirt`\n1125\tjerseys, `sleeves: 'short'`, hair, headgear, a real palette); `propSize: 1.3`; textured floors (`floorTex`) and walls\n1126\t(`face`, `roof`); 3-8 props per screen (corner flags, the dugouts' benches, water bottles on the touchline, kit bags,\n1127\tcones, floodlight towers, sponsor boards, the sin bin, cameramen on the touchline as small Humanoids with a box camera);\n1128\teffects on every hit; `E.font.title` logos with 3-4 colour gradients and depth; light in every night scene; portraits in\n1129\tevery dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\n1130\tnot with NES ones. Performance is out of scope (TASK.md): favour detail (full crowds, lights, particles, shadows) over\n1131\tframe rate.\n1132\t\n1133\t### 10.2 Characters\n1134\t\n1135\tColours shaded with `E.tones` where drawn by hand. Each team's players differ in build, size, hair, skin and headgear so\n1136\tthey read as people, not clones; jersey colours carry the team. Mud builds up on kits at Muddington (`rig.C.cloth` and\n1137\t`pants` mixed toward `#5a3a1e` by `mud` 0-0.6, restored at the next match). Stunned players get orbiting stars (a\n1138\tthree-frame string sprite) over their heads. The ball carrier gets a subtle white outline in busy moments.\n1139\t\n1140\t### 10.3 New art assets (all drawn by code)\n1141\t\n1142\t| Asset | How |\n1143\t|---|---|\n1144\t| Oval ball (laces, panel lines; 16 turns) | `E.sprite` strings 9x6, drawn with `rot` (cached), end-over-end flicker for kicks |\n1145\t| Goalposts with pads, crossbar | `r.queue` lines and rects projected with `r.w`, depth-sorted with the ball |\n1146\t| Pitch markings, in-goal crest | `floorTex` |\n1147\t| Stands, crowd, flags, banners | TileMap tiers + `r.queue` figures (as the sports kit), `banner` props in team colours |\n1148\t| Sponsor boards with text | south boards as cut walls with text drawn on their faces through `r.queue` |\n1149\t| Floodlight towers, jumbotron (shows score, portraits, TRY!) | custom shapes (`docs/ASSETS.md` format) or `r.queue` boxes; the jumbotron draws `rig.drawPortrait` |\n1150\t| Skylines per venue | the TileMap has `outside: false`; each draw paints `r.sky([...])`, then the venue's silhouettes (hills, cranes, chimneys, towers) anchored to the far stand's projected top edge (`r.w` of its back corners), then the map, so the stand meets the skyline whatever the camera does |\n1151\t| Sin bin dumpster | a custom shape (green metal box, lid, SIN BIN stencil); the binned player drawn inside |\n1152\t| Kicking tee, cones, tackle bags, corner flags, water bottles, kit bags | small custom shapes or string sprites |\n1153\t| Power-up sprites (pie, pads, boot, jersey, horn) | string sprites 12-14 px with a glint |\n1154\t| Captain Clucky | an `E.Blob` (`R: 14`, white and yellow, `wings`, `feet`, a red comb and beak drawn over it) |\n1155\t| Flame grates and jets, scorch decals, lightning bolt | decals, `particles.fire`, `px.line` zig-zags, emissive queue items |\n1156\t| Crests (5 teams), the Channel Thud bug, the MEGA CUP trophy | string sprites and a custom shape |\n1157\t| Button badges (PlayStation, Xbox, keycaps, mouse) | string sprites (§6.4) |\n1158\t| Clubhouse, tunnel, podium sets | small TileMaps with store props (`kenney-furniture`, `kaykit-restaurant-bits` via `E.addAssets`; check with `tools/asset-find.mjs`) |\n1159\t\n1160\t### 10.4 Effects\n1161\t\n1162\tTackles: dust (`particles.dust`), grass divots (`bits` in greens), mud splats (`bits` browns) at Muddington. Big hits:\n1163\t`game.hitFx` (no damage number: leave `damage` out and check none shows), `freeze(.08)`, `shake(4)`, sparks. Monster\n1164\thits: `freeze(.12)`, `flash`, `shake(6)`, a ring, a 1.1x zoom punch tweened back, a \"WHUMP\" text particle. Tries:\n1165\tconfetti `bits` in the scorers' colours, crowd jump, fireworks at night (`particles.explosion` high in the sky),\n1166\tlasers at the Megadome. ON FIRE and supers: `fire` particles trailing, emissive glow. Weather from `game.weather`.\n1167\t\n1168\t### 10.5 HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n1169\t\n1170\t| Where | What |\n1171\t|---|---|\n1172\t| Top left | The TV score bug: crests, three-letter names (MUD, BAD, GUL, IRN, MEG), scores, the half and the sevens clock (with HOOTER flashing past time); each team's HYPE bar under its name (flashing \"△ SUPER\" when full); sin-bin timers as small dumpster icons with seconds |\n1173\t| Top centre | Event banners (`E.font.title` scale 3-4, popped in with a tween, 1.2-2 s): TRY!, MONSTER HIT!, LINE BREAK!, ON FIRE!, SIN BIN!, REF DOWN!, PUSHOVER TRY!, DROP GOAL!, CONVERTED!, WIDE!, KNOCK-ON, FORWARD!, ADVANTAGE, HOOTER! |\n1174\t| Top right | The radar: the pitch small, dots in team colours, white ball, controlled players ringed |\n1175\t| Bottom corners | One card per human seat: the controlled player's live portrait, nickname, turbo bar, power-up icon and seconds |\n1176\t| Bottom centre | Context prompts (two or three badges with a word: \"{b:x} STEP  {b:sq} FEND  {b:ci} KICK\"), above the commentary lower-third |\n1177\t| In the world | Seat rings and chevrons; L1 / R1 badges over the two receivers; the landing ring of every kick; offside lines (dashed, team colour, \"OFFSIDE\" at the ends) during rucks, scrums and lineouts; the ref's sight cone; the \"USE IT\" ring; off-screen arrows (`r.marker`) for the ball and each controlled player |\n1178\t| Set pieces | Big centred widgets: the scrum's SET ring and push bar (with both teams' colours), the lineout's three pod buttons and the throw needle, the kick meter (vertical, with the sweet band), the set kick's reticle and wind arrow, the penalty choice's three cards |\n1179\t\n1180\t### 10.6 Menus and screens: 10-foot rules\n1181\t\n1182\t- Everything readable at 3 m on a TV: body text never below the 5x7 font at scale 1 on the ps1 buffer (about 30 TV\n1183\t  pixels high at 1080p); menu entries at scale 2; titles 3-4. No more than seven choices on a screen, and no tables of\n1184\t  numbers: results show four big numbers, team cards three bars.\n1185\t- Focus is unmistakable (a glowing box, ▸ markers, a sound); d-pad and stick move it, ✕ picks, ○ goes back; the mouse\n1186\t  over an item moves the focus, a click picks it (E.Menu does both); every card-style screen does the same with\n1187\t  `input.pointer()` / `input.clicked()`.\n1188\t- The standard HTML pause, settings and controls screens (engine's `E.Shell`) stay (they are the engine's standard\n1189\t  features), restyled for a TV with CSS in the page: `.esh { font-size: 20px }`, `.esh button { font-size: 18px;\n1190\t  padding: 14px 20px; min-height: 56px }`, `.esh-mod { width: min(720px, 100%) }`, `.esh h2 { font-size: 34px }`,\n1191\t  `.esh-row { padding: 12px 0 }`, the theme in team colours (accent `#f0c040`, paper `rgba(16,20,28,.92)`).\n1192\t- Every screen shows its prompts with the badges of the device used last.\n1193\t\n1194\t### 10.7 Camera direction (TV flourishes)\n1195\t\n1196\tWalk-outs before kick-off (both teams jog out of the tunnel to the halfway line; captains shake hands; 6 s, skippable);\n1197\ta slow push-in on the kicker before a set kick; the replay angle; the crowd and jumbotron cut-ins at scores (a 1 s\n1198\tpicture-in-picture of the scorer's portrait on the jumbotron); the camera never shakes during menus.\n1199\t\n1200\t---\n1201\t\n1202\t## 11. Animation\n1203\t\n1204\t### 11.1 How (native system, extended)\n1205\t\n1206\t- Everything is the engine's Humanoid rig, driven by continuous values (`rig.update(dt, state)`).\n1207\t- **Paired and multi-body moves** are `E.ACTIONS` entries (`{ beats, setup, at }` like the engine's `takedown`), run by\n1208\t  `new E.Action(name, { body, other })`; the action moves the bodies and gives `rigState()` / `otherState()`.\n1209\t- **New poses** are `rig.solvePose` wrappers that move joints after the base solve (as Emberdeep does): the ball carry,\n1210\t  arms-out celebrations, the scrum bind, the lineout lift, the referee's signals.\n1211\t- **New strikes** are attack specs in the `E.MOVES` format with `hand`, `kick`, `lunge`, `hop`, `crouch`, `lean`,\n1212\t  `twist`, `blade: 0`.\n1213\t- **The anim record:** each player's `anim` in `MatchState` is what the rig needs, compactly: `{ m (move id), ph\n1214\t  (phase), u, p (pose id), dn (down 0-1), air, fl (flip 0-1), cr (crouch), ex (expression), hu (hurt), arms (custom pose\n1215\t  id), w (pose weight) }`. The host and replays fill it from actions; online clients and replays feed it to rigs. A\n1216\t  player who is just running has no `anim` beyond velocity (the gait comes from `vx, vy`).\n1217\t- Check every new move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` contact sheets (wind-up, strike, follow-through, clean settle) and with\n1218\t  `rig.debug(r)` and `game.timeScale = .25`.\n1219\t\n1220\t### 11.2 The rugby move set\n1221\t\n1222\t| Move | Built as |\n1223\t|---|---|\n1224\t| Carry | `solvePose` wrap: the ball arm's hand at the far hip, elbow tucked; two hands on the ball when a pass is coming (the last 0.2 s before the pass button is likely, i.e. when a receiver is lined up) |\n1225\t| Pass (short, long) | a spec: `hand: 'both'`, a swing across the body from the far hip to the receiver's side at chest height, `twist`, `wind .06 active .08 recover .18`; long: bigger wind and twist |\n1226\t| Offload | a one-handed pop (`hand: 'L'`, short) while falling in the tackle |\n1227\t| Dummy | the pass spec stopped at the end of the wind, then the carry |\n1228\t| Sidestep | a lateral hop (`hop`), the body leaning away, the legs crossing (velocity impulse) |\n1229\t| Spin | `spin: true` with the ball held in both hands, `blade: 0` |\n1230\t| Fend | `thrust` with `hand: 'L'`, `blade: 0`, held (`hold .6`), stiff arm at shoulder height |\n1231\t| Tackle (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.tackle`: beats lunge .12, wrap .15, fall .35, ground .3: the tackler drives low (crouch, lean) with arms wrapping the carrier's waist; both go down (`down` 0→1), the carrier back or sideways; dust |\n1232\t| Big hit (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.bigHit`: charge .1, impact .06, launch .5, land .3: the carrier flies (an arc, `flip` 0→1), lands heavily (`land: 1`), slides; the hitter stands over him with a flex (`pose: 'guard'`, `expr: 'shout'`) |\n1233\t| Dive tackle (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.diveTackle`: the diver flies flat (`down: 1` with `z` above the ground: a superman dive), arms forward; the carrier trips and falls forward |\n1234\t| Try dive | `E.ACTIONS.tryDive`: the carrier dives flat with the ball held out, slides 12 u on the grass, a puff of dust |\n1235\t| Get up | the engine's `getUp` |\n1236\t| Ruck | bodies bent at the hips (`crouch`, a lean), heads down, legs churning (`run: 1`), one or two lying in it (`down: .6`); a dust cloud over the pile |\n1237\t| Scrum | three a side bound in a row (`solvePose`: arms over the neighbours' shoulders), bent flat-backed, `run` in place while pushing; a collapse is `down: 1` |\n1238\t| Lineout lift (three bodies) | the jumper rises to z 60 with arms up (`pose: 'cheer'` blend), two lifters crouched below with arms up holding (`pose: 'cast'` with the hands raised); timed together by one action on the jumper and one on each lifter |\n1239\t| Lineout throw | a two-handed overhead throw (`hand: 'both'`, from behind the head) |\n1240\t| Catch high ball | `air` with arms up |\n1241\t| Punt, grubber, drop kick | the engine's `kick` with the ball drawn from the hands to the foot through the wind-up; the drop kick bounces the ball once first |\n1242\t| Place kick | three run-up steps on an angle, the `kick` with a big lean and follow-through (`hold .8`); the kicker's crouched pre-kick stance beforehand |\n1243\t| Celebrations (one per player, from a pool of six) | knee slide (`down: .4` travelling), aeroplane arms (`solvePose` arms out, banking), the flex (`pose: 'guard'`, `expr: 'shout'`), the cocky one (`pose: 'hips'`), the bow, the belly flop (`down: 1` with a bounce) |\n1244\t| Referee signals | try (arm up, pointing down), penalty (arm out and up toward the team), advantage (arm out flat, held), scrum (arm out low), the card held high (a yellow or red rect at `rig.hand('R')`), the whistle at the mouth |\n1245\t| Stunned, toasted, zapped | `hurt`, a head sway (`solvePose` small roll), stars; toasted: colours darkened briefly, smoke; zapped: the skeleton rig drawn for two frames |\n1246\t| Sin bin sulk | inside the dumpster, `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'angry'` |\n1247\t| Walk-out and handshake | a jog; captains shake hands (`solvePose`: right hands meet) |\n1248\t\n1249\t---\n1250\t\n1251\t## 12. Audio (all in code: the engine's chip synth and Web Audio; no files)\n1252\t\n1253\t### 12.1 Music (song objects for `game.audio.music`, with named layers for `audio.layer`)\n1254\t\n1255\t| Song | Where | Character | Layers |\n1256\t|---|---|---|---|\n1257\t| \"Thugby Turbo!\" | title, menus | glam-rock stomp, 152 bpm, square lead, saw bass, handclaps; the crowd chants \"THUG-BY!\" on the 2 and 4 | `base`, `chant` |\n1258\t| \"Mud and Glory\" | Muddington | brass-band march on pulses, 126 bpm | `base`, `drums` (in when the ball is in an opponents' 22), `hype` (a team's meter full / ON FIRE) |\n1259\t| \"Grumble Shanty\" | Port Grumble | a shanty in a rolling 6/8 feel (steps: 3), accordion-ish pulse12 | same three |\n1260\t| \"Forge Floor\" | The Furnace | industrial: low saw ostinato, anvil hits (noise + triangle ping), 132 bpm | same three |\n1261\t| \"Megadome Mayhem\" | the final | minor-key, fast drums, arpeggios, 160 bpm | same three |\n1262\t| \"Half-Time Pub Piano\" | halftime, clubhouse | honky-tonk, triangle + pulse | none |\n1263\t| \"Third Half\" | credits | the club song, a babble choir over it | none |\n1264\t| Stings (`audio.sting`) | | try fanfare; monster-hit brass stab; ON FIRE riff; yellow-card sad trombone; drop-goal ding-dong; victory jingle; defeat jingle; kick-off drum roll | |\n1265\t\n1266\t### 12.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices)\n1267\t\n1268\tWhistle (short, long, triple for full time), the HOOTER (a loud square and saw blare), tackle thud (low sine + noise),\n1269\tbig-hit crunch (noise burst + falling sine + boom), pass whoosh, catch slap, punt thump, grubber tap, ball bounce (a\n1270\thollow \"bok\": triangle 300→180), DOINK (triangle 1200 ringing), scrum engage crunch, ruck grunts (babble), air horn\n1271\t(square chord), pie munch, turbo whoosh and sputter, super charge (a rising arpeggio), flame jet roar (filtered noise\n1272\tsweep), lightning crack and thunder, chicken squawk (square, vibrato up and down), mud squelch, card ding and the crowd\n1273\tboo, the slow hand-clap, menu select/confirm/cancel (engine presets).\n1274\t\n1275\t### 12.3 Voices: Animalese-style babble\n1276\t\n1277\t- Patch 4 gives `E.Dialog.onLetter(ch, i, text)`. `TT.babble.letter(ch, speaker)` plays one syllable per letter: letters\n1278\t  map to semitone offsets (vowels lower and 30% longer), `freq = speaker.base × 2^(semi/12)`, a 45-75 ms voice of the\n1279\t  speaker's wave (`sfx({ wave, freq, to: freq × 0.94, dur, vol, vib })`), louder and higher for capitals, a rise over the\n1280\t  last three letters before `?`, a jump on `!`; spaces and punctuation are silent beats.\n1281\t- Speakers: Barry (square, base 330, fast), Ros (triangle, 220, measured), Gristle (saw, 140, gravel: a second voice an\n1282\t  octave down), Nigel (pulse12, 260, nasal), Big Dave (triangle, 160), each player (pitch from size and build:\n1283\t  80-300), Nan (pulse, 380 with vibrato), Sir Rupert (square, 200, slow), Big Unit (saw, 70, one roar), the stadium PA\n1284\t  (square, 180, with an echo: the same syllable 180 ms later at half volume).\n1285\t- In play: players grunt short babble bursts on tackles, rucks and scrums; the referee babbles his calls; the crowd\n1286\t  chants in a choir of five detuned voices on the beat (`audio.onBeat`).\n1287\t\n1288\t### 12.4 The crowd\n1289\t\n1290\tA looping bed of filtered noise whose volume follows excitement (ball near a try line, a line break, a big hit) with\n1291\tswells, roars on scores, a groan on misses, boos on cards, the slow hand-clap at set kicks; a Crowd volume slider in\n1292\tSound.\n1293\t\n1294\t---\n1295\t\n1296\t## 13. Attract mode\n1297\t\n1298\t- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it. One `new E.Arcade(game, { id:\n1299\t  'thugby', idle: 10, demo: 300, scores: 8, hud: false })`; those scenes call `arcade.attract(dt)` each step; when\n1300\t  `arcade.phase` turns `'demo'` they `game.go('match', { attract: true })`; the director calls `arcade.endDemo()` and\n1301\t  goes back to the title at its end (the `'scores'` phase then shows the records with `arcade.drawTable`); an exit by\n1302\t  input calls `arcade.wake()`. Our own idle check (below) also counts mouse movement and sticks.\n1303\t- It is a CPU vs CPU match (teams and venue rotate through all four venues across loops) with cheats on: no clock,\n1304\t  hype on demand, events forced. A **director** (`game.script`) walks a showcase list, using the same `game.debug.force`\n1305\t  calls as the dev panel, each step when the previous one finished (or 12 s passed):\n1306\t  1. walk-out and kick-off; 2. a run with a sidestep and a fend; 3. a pass chain along the line with a dummy; 4. a\n1307\t  MONSTER HIT and its replay; 5. a ruck with a jackal; 6. a knock-on and a scrum; 7. a kick to touch and a lineout; 8. a\n1308\t  power-up thrown on and taken; 9. the venue's hazard; 10. THUNDER RUN to a try, the celebration, the replay; 11. the\n1309\t  conversion in the kicker's camera; 12. a cheap shot behind the ref's back, then one he sees: a yellow card and the sin\n1310\t  bin; 13. a player ON FIRE scoring; 14. a drop goal. Then the logo and the records for 8 s, then the title.\n1311\t- Overlays: \"DEMO\" top centre, a blinking \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (or \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" on touch-only), the\n1312\t  logo small in a corner; the HUD and commentary as in a real match.\n1313\t- Any input exits at once: a key, a mouse button or movement over 8 px, a pad button or a stick past 0.5, a tap. The\n1314\t  exiting input is consumed (`consumeAll`) so it does not also pick a menu item. It returns to the title.\n1315\t- Attract never writes saves or records and never runs in an AI Hub session.\n1316\t\n1317\t---\n1318\t\n1319\t## 14. Dev mode"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b392508-0a9c-4851-a1e8-b9fce2e4b886","uuid":"7806c2e2-3ef6-4159-beed-7f18f135606e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:56:35.680Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-065619__xa7e588/work/PLAN.md","content":"Also: COACH GORDON GRISTLE (ex-prop, 60s: bulky 1.3, bald with grey fringe, flat cap `hat: 'cap'`, `outfit: 'coat'`\nbrown), BIG DAVE (the bus driver: bulky 1.35, beanie-like `hat: 'band'`, hi-vis jacket `coat` `#e8e030`).\n\n**BRAMBLEWICK BADGERS** (round one; a village side). Home: black `#24242a`, trim white `#f0f0f0`, shorts white. Away:\nwhite, trim black, shorts black. Crest: a badger's striped face. Style: cautious (aggression .3, pass .4, kick .5,\ncheap shots .05). Difficulty base: Rookie.\n\n| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Edna \"Nan\" Pemberton (captain, 74) | Prop | bulky 1.25, `hunch: .2` | short grey hair, knitted scrum cap cream | 3 8 6 4 8 |\n| 2 | Barnaby \"Barn Door\" Pike | Prop | bulky 1.38 | bald, ruddy | 3 9 3 2 7 |\n| 3 | Wilf Hollins | Hooker | bulky 1.2 | short brown | 4 7 5 3 6 |\n| 4 | Pip Tanner | Scrum-half | heroic 1.0 | spiky ginger | 7 3 7 5 5 |\n| 5 | Clementine Ashby | Fly-half | heroic 1.1 | ponytail blonde | 5 4 7 8 4 |\n| 6 | Ollie \"Badger\" Brock | Centre | heroic 1.25 | short black, grey streak | 6 7 5 3 6 |\n| 7 | Tilly Fenwick | Wing | heroic 1.08 | long black | 8 3 6 4 4 |\n\n**PORT GRUMBLE GULLS** (quarter-final; a flashy harbour side). Home: white `#f4f4f0`, trim teal `#1fa89a`, shorts navy\n`#1e2a50`. Away: teal, trim white, navy. Crest: a gull with a chip. Style: running and kicking (aggression .45, pass\n.75, kick .5, cheap shots .1). Difficulty base: Pro, reaction 0.3 s. Mascot: CAPTAIN CLUCKY.\n\n| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Sal \"Salty\" Pereira | Prop | bulky 1.32 | short black | 4 8 5 3 7 |\n| 2 | Kenji \"Kipper\" Ito | Hooker | bulky 1.2 | spiky black | 6 7 7 3 6 |\n| 3 | Mo \"Anchor\" Haddad | Prop | bulky 1.38 | bald | 4 9 4 2 8 |\n| 4 | Lulu Fairweather | Scrum-half | heroic 1.02 | ponytail red | 8 4 9 6 5 |\n| 5 | Jonty \"Silky\" Swift (captain) | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | long golden, a headband | 7 5 9 9 4 |\n| 6 | Dexter \"Jet\" Okoro | Centre | heroic 1.25 | short, dark skin | 8 7 7 4 6 |\n| 7 | Bree \"Breeze\" Lindqvist | Wing | heroic 1.1 | long platinum | 10 4 8 5 4 |\n\n**FURNACE FORGE IRONSIDES** (semi-final; foundry hard men and women). Home: charcoal `#3a3a44`, trim molten orange\n`#f07a1e`, shorts black. Away: orange, trim charcoal. Crest: an anvil in flames. Style: big hitters (aggression .85,\npass .35, kick .25, cheap shots .35, line speed fast). Difficulty base: Pro. Most wear scrum caps in orange.\n\n| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Grigor \"The Kiln\" Petrov | Prop | bulky 1.4 | bald, a soot smudge (skin darker) | 4 10 3 2 9 |\n| 2 | \"Rusty\" Nailor | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | short rust-red | 5 8 5 3 8 |\n| 3 | Bertha \"Big Bertha\" Blunt | Prop | bulky 1.4 | ponytail black | 4 10 4 2 9 |\n| 4 | Smudge Cole | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | spiky black | 7 5 7 5 6 |\n| 5 | Ingot Ingram | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | short blond | 6 6 7 8 6 |\n| 6 | Adaeze \"Anvil\" Okafor (captain) | Centre | bulky 1.32 | short black, dark skin | 7 9 6 3 9 |\n| 7 | Flint Mackay | Wing | heroic 1.12 | spiky grey | 9 6 6 4 6 |\n\n**MEGACORP MAULERS** (the grand final; a billionaire's bought-in super team; unlocked after the cup). Home: gold\n`#e8c040`, trim purple `#5a2a8a`, shorts `#3a1a5a`. Away: purple, trim gold. Crest: a gold \"M\" in a purple diamond.\nStyle: everything (aggression .7, pass .6, kick .45, cheap shots .25, supers eagerly). Difficulty base: Legend. Owner:\nSIR RUPERT GOLDBRICK (cutscenes only: heroic 1.15, `outfit: 'coat'` purple, `hat: 'crown'` gold, a monocle drawn as one\npixel ring).\n\n| # | Name \"Nickname\" | Role | Build, size | Look | SPD POW HND KCK TKL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"BIG UNIT\" Brannigan (captain, the boss) | Prop | bulky **2.0** | bald, a gold headband | 6 12 6 3 10 (POW beyond the scale on purpose) |\n| 2 | Leverage Lou | Hooker | bulky 1.25 | slicked short | 6 8 7 3 7 |\n| 3 | \"Bonus\" Barrington | Prop | bulky 1.38 | short blond | 5 9 5 2 8 |\n| 4 | Synergy Jones | Scrum-half | heroic 1.05 | ponytail violet | 9 5 9 6 6 |\n| 5 | Chad Sterling III | Fly-half | heroic 1.15 | long gold, smug | 7 6 9 10 5 |\n| 6 | Vance Capitale | Centre | heroic 1.28 | spiky black | 8 8 7 5 7 |\n| 7 | Hedge Fundsworth | Wing | heroic 1.12 | short silver | 10 5 8 6 5 |\n\nBIG UNIT is `immovable` (gang tackle needed), his fend flings tacklers 40 u, all his tackles are big hits, and his\nsuper is the UNIT TRAIN (a 6 s Thunder Run). He gets a spotlight entrance.\n\nCommentators and referee (portraits only, plus the referee on the pitch): BARRY BELLOWS (heroic 1.1, comb-over, a\nblazer `coat` maroon, headset drawn as a dark band), ROS RUCKER (heroic 1.1, short grey bob, cauliflower ear: a pink\npixel blob; blazer navy), NIGEL BLEWITT (heroic 1.1, black kit with green trim, short brown hair, big ears).\n\n### 9.2 Venues (data: `{ id, name, time, weather, wind, lights, grass, stands, crowd, boards, skyline, hazard, music }`)\n\n| Venue | Look | Skyline beyond the far stand | Boards (fictional sponsors) | Music |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Muddington Park** (Mudlarks' home; the training ground too, by day without rain) | overcast day; a small wooden stand (`face: 'plank'`) and grass banks; the Muddy Duck pub behind the east in-goal | low hills, a church spire, drizzle | THE MUDDY DUCK · PIES & PINTS, BIG DAVE'S BUSES, CHANNEL THUD | \"Mud and Glory\" |\n| **Port Grumble Docks** | dusk, orange sky; a concrete stand; shipping containers stacked behind one end | cranes, a lighthouse, gulls wheeling | SEAGULL-PROOF CHIPS, KRAKEN INSURANCE, GRUMBLE'S GRAVY | \"Grumble Shanty\" |\n| **The Furnace** | night, floodlights (4 towers); black steel stands (`face: 'stone'` dark); glowing grates | chimneys belching sparks, a red glow | FORGEWORKS STEEL, TURBO TONIC, MEGA MEAT PIES | \"Forge Floor\" |\n| **The Megadome** | night storm; a huge gold and purple bowl, a jumbotron on the far stand, lasers on tries | city towers, a GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS sign | GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS, CHANNEL THUD, TURBO TONIC | \"Megadome Mayhem\" |\n\nLighting (every scene is lit, as the look target asks): day `lights.enabled = true` with ambient 0.95 and a warm tint;\ndusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool under each tower, `lights.add` every\ndraw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames. Crowd: stand tiles hold two figures\neach (as the sports kit) in the two teams' colours (home 70%), bobbing; they jump on scores and boo cards; a Mexican wave\nrolls round when play is stopped longer than 8 s. Floodlight towers: tall lamp props or custom shapes on the stand\ncorners.\n\n### 9.3 The Mega Cup: story beats and script\n\nWrite all story text in this voice: broadcast hype, pub banter, clichés turned up to eleven. Lines are `E.Story` nodes\n(data in `03-data-content.js`), spoken with portraits and babble voices; ALL CAPS shouts shake (`{shake}`); pauses with\n`{w=.4}`. The lines below are the spine; add up to two more per scene in the same style, no more.\n\n1. **Prologue: the Muddy Duck** (clubhouse set: plank floor `E.tex.planks`, plaster walls, a bar of counters, barrels,\n   stools, a dartboard, a pie warmer glowing, warm lamps; threequarter view, zoom 1.5).\n   - BIG DAVE: \"So I'm filling in the form, right. 'Mega Cup.' I thought it was a tea thing.\"\n   - GRISTLE: \"It's the TURBO SEVENS MEGA CUP, Dave. Live on Channel Thud. Against teams with dieticians.\"\n   - THE FRIDGE: \"We've got a dietician.\" *(nods at the pie warmer)*\n   - GRISTLE: \"Gristle's Rule Number One: nobody laughs at the Mudlarks. Rule Number Two: we train. Now. Yes, you too,\n     Dave.\"\n   - Choice: TRAIN (→ training) / SKIP TO THE CUP.\n2. **Round one vs Bramblewick Badgers, Muddington Park** (pitch-side set: the two captains face to face at halfway,\n   zoom 1.4).\n   - BARRY: \"Welcome to a damp Muddington Park, where the Mudlarks open their Mega Cup against the Bramblewick Badgers!\"\n   - ROS: \"Damp is generous, Barry. I've seen drier rivers.\"\n   - NAN PEMBERTON: \"I've propped since before your dad had teeth, sonny. I've had hip replacements tougher than you.\"\n   - GRISTLE: \"She's seventy-four, lads. Do NOT go easy on her. She bites.\"\n   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"Rule Three: hold the ball. Rule Four: see Rule Three.\"\n   - Won: BARRY: \"The Mudlarks are through! Ros, are they any good?\" ROS: \"They're... present, Barry.\"\n3. **Quarter-final vs Port Grumble Gulls, Port Grumble Docks.**\n   - JONTY SWIFT: \"Gorgeous evening. Gorgeous ground. Gorgeous me. Do try to keep up, darlings.\"\n   - GRISTLE: \"Watch the wind. Watch the chicken. Don't ask about the chicken.\"\n   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"Pass it like it's hot. It IS hot. It's Port Grumble. Everything here's been deep-fried.\"\n   - Won: ROS: \"That chicken has more caps than I do.\"\n4. **Semi-final vs Furnace Forge Ironsides, The Furnace.**\n   - ANVIL OKAFOR: \"We forge champions here. Everyone else, we melt down for scrap.\"\n   - GRISTLE: \"Don't stand on the glowing bits. Wheels. Wheels, look at me. The GLOWING bits.\"\n   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"They hit hard? Hit harder. Then hide behind Tiny.\"\n   - Won: BARRY: \"A PUB TEAM IN THE MEGA CUP FINAL! Somebody pinch me!\" ROS: \"Gladly, Barry.\"\n5. **Grand final vs Megacorp Maulers, The Megadome** (tunnel set; lights down, a spotlight for BIG UNIT).\n   - SIR RUPERT GOLDBRICK: \"Charming little pub team. I'll buy the lot of you. The pub, the pies, the muddy bird. Name\n     your price.\"\n   - THE FRIDGE: \"Not for sale.\"\n   - GRISTLE: \"The pies are for sale. Two-fifty. WE'RE not.\"\n   - BIG UNIT: \"*(one long babble roar)*\" BARRY: \"BIG UNIT BRANNIGAN! Two metres of pure invoice!\" ROS: \"You'll need two\n     men to bring him down, minimum. Bring a ladder.\"\n   - Halftime, GRISTLE: \"I've written the big speech. In my head. It's very moving. Pretend I said it. NOW GET OUT\n     THERE!\"\n6. **Victory** (podium set: confetti, fireworks, the MEGA CUP trophy, a gaudy golden cup twice a man's height).\n   - BARRY: \"THE MUDDINGTON MUDLARKS ARE MEGA CUP CHAMPIONS! A PUB TEAM, ROS! A PUB TEAM!\"\n   - ROS: \"I need a lie down, Barry.\"\n   - SIR RUPERT: \"I'll buy the trophy, then.\" GRISTLE: \"Rule Five: no.\"\n7. **The third half** (back at the Muddy Duck; everyone cheering, Nan Pemberton and Captain Clucky included; the cast\n   sings the club song in a babble choir with lyrics on screen):\n   *\"Oh Muddington, oh Muddington, your mud is in my soul / We lost our boots, we lost our teeth, we never lost the\n   ball...\"* GRISTLE: \"Last orders!\" → credits.\n- **A lost match:** GRISTLE: \"Rule Six: we go again.\" → E.Arcade `continue(10)`: CONTINUE? (✕ retries the match with a\n  new seed; at zero, back to the cup hub with the match still NEXT).\n\nDrawn-out cutscenes are skippable (△); a skipped scene never blocks progress.\n\n### 9.4 Training Ground (Coach Gristle's drills)\n\nEach drill is a match scene with a scripted setup, a goal predicate, a prompt line with glyphs, and a **SHOW ME** (△)\nbutton where the coach's AI does it once (\"Watch me, you muppets\"). Its `auto` script is the same one the tests use to\nprove it can be completed. ○ / Esc leaves; a failed attempt resets in 1 s.\n\n| # | Drill | Setup | Goal | Teaches |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | LEGS | you with the ball at your 22, cones to the try line | run to the line on turbo, dive (✕) over | moving, turbo, grounding |\n| 2 | HANDS | you and four runners in a line | five passes, both directions, then a long pass; a forward pass to Wheels shows the whistle | L1/R1, long pass, the backwards rule |\n| 3 | FEET | three tackle bags and a defender | sidestep twice, spin once, fend the defender | ✕ sidestep and spin, □ fend |\n| 4 | HIT | a runner coming at you, then another | a tackle, a BIG HIT (hold ✕), a dive tackle (□), switching (○ and L1/R1) | defence |\n| 5 | RUCK | three tackles in a row | win two rucks by mashing, then jackal one (□) | breakdown |\n| 6 | BOOT | you with the ball | a grubber into the in-goal and chase it; a punt into touch; a drop goal from 30 m | kicking |\n| 7 | SET PIECES | the forwards | win a scrum (✕ on SET, alternate L1/R1), win a lineout (call a pod, throw) | scrum, lineout |\n| 8 | POSTS | a try just scored out wide | convert it: place, aim, power | set kicks |\n| 9 | TURBO TIME | hype full, a meat pie on the pitch | take the pie, then THUNDER RUN through three defenders to score | power-ups, supers |\n\n### 9.5 Commentary\n\nThe director listens to the bus, picks a line by category with priorities (a try beats a pass), cooldowns (no category\ntwice in 6 s, no line twice in a match: shuffle bags), alternates Barry (play-by-play, first) and Ros (colour, a beat\nlater, 40% of the time), fills `{$player}` (nickname), `{$team}`, `{$score}`, `{$venue}`, and shows it on the radio\ndialog (`modal: false`, `auto: 2.2`, at the bottom, portraits). Setting: Commentary On / Text only / Off. Write at least\nsix lines per category in this voice:\n\n| Category | Lines (Barry unless marked Ros) |\n|---|---|\n| kick-off | \"And we're underway at {$venue}!\" · \"Big boot to get us going!\" · Ros: \"Here we go. Mind the mud.\" |\n| try | \"HE'S GONE OVER! TRY TIME!\" · \"Under the sticks! You could drive a bus through that gap!\" · \"Dotted down! {$player}, take a bow!\" · \"In at the corner! Somebody check the paint on that touchline!\" · Ros: \"Textbook. If the textbook was written by a hurricane.\" |\n| big hit | \"OH, THAT'S A BIG ONE!\" · \"He'll feel that in the morning. And the morning after.\" · \"Absolutely SHUDDERING!\" · Ros: \"I felt that in my old knee, Barry.\" |\n| monster hit | \"MONSTER HIT! That's gone into orbit!\" · \"Put him in Row Z!\" · \"Somebody get that man a postcode, he's lost!\" |\n| sidestep / spin | \"Left him for dead!\" · \"Feet like a ballroom dancer!\" · Ros: \"Lovely footwork. Questionable haircut. Lovely footwork.\" |\n| fend | \"HAND-OFF! Right in the chops!\" · \"He's fended him into next week!\" |\n| dummy | \"Oh, the dummy! They've bought it, the whole shop!\" |\n| line break | \"He's through! There's daylight!\" · \"The line's been cut like a birthday cake!\" |\n| knock-on | \"Knock-on. Butter fingers.\" · \"Dropped it like a hot pie!\" |\n| forward pass | \"Forward! The ref's not having that.\" · Ros: \"Forward by a country mile, Barry.\" |\n| ruck / jackal / turnover | \"JACKAL! He's pinched it!\" · \"Turnover! Stolen like a pie at a buffet!\" |\n| scrum | \"Crouch... bind... SET! And they've hit like freight trains!\" · Ros: \"That scrum's going backwards, and so is their dignity.\" |\n| pushover try | \"PUSHOVER TRY! They've shoved them over the line like a wardrobe!\" |\n| lineout | \"He's been lifted so high he can see his house!\" · \"Stolen at the lineout! Cheeky!\" |\n| conversion made / missed | \"Straight between the sticks!\" · \"Bang! Two more!\" · \"Wide! Hooked it like a fisherman.\" · \"DOINK! Off the upright!\" |\n| drop goal | \"DROP GOAL! Cheeky, cheeky!\" |\n| penalty / advantage | \"Penalty! The ref's arm is out!\" · \"Advantage being played...\" · \"Advantage over.\" |\n| unseen cheap shot | \"Ooh... the ref's missed that one completely.\" · \"What the ref doesn't see, Ros...\" Ros: \"...is still assault, Barry.\" |\n| yellow / red | \"YELLOW CARD! Off to the sin bin, and I mean an actual bin!\" · \"RED CARD! Early bath!\" |\n| ref down | \"THE REF'S DOWN! Anything goes, Barry!\" (Ros says it; Barry: \"Anything goes, Ros!\") |\n| on fire | \"HE'S ON FIRE!\" · \"Somebody call the fire brigade! Actually, don't, let it burn!\" |\n| super | \"THUNDER RUN! Get out of the way!\" · \"HURRICANE HIT INCOMING!\" |\n| power-up | \"Somebody's chucked a meat pie on the pitch!\" Ros: \"Is that... gravy?\" · \"IRON SHOULDERS! He's a walking wardrobe!\" · \"The MEGA BOOT! Stand well back!\" · \"Grease jersey! Slippery as a sardine!\" · \"AIR HORN! The crowd's gone barmy!\" |\n| hazards | \"It's CAPTAIN CLUCKY! The mascot's on the pitch again!\" · \"Mind the flames! That's a well-done winger!\" · \"Lightning strike! That's one way to clear a ruck!\" · \"He's in the mud! Half man, half puddle!\" |\n| hooter / half / full / sudden death | \"There's the hooter! Ball has to go dead!\" · \"Half-time here at {$venue}: {$score}.\" · \"FULL TIME! {$team} win it, {$score}!\" · \"That's it! Somebody get the kettle on!\" · \"Golden point! Next score wins the lot!\" |\n\n### 9.6 Records and unlocks\n\nE.Arcade tables (`id: 'thugby'`), modes `margin`, `tries`, `hit` (metres flown × 10), seeded with ten fictional\nentries each (initials of the cast: \"NAN 34\", \"BIG 12\"...). After an Exhibition or cup match, any qualifying number\nopens the initials wheel. Unlocks as in §8.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Art direction and presentation\n\n### 10.1 The engine's look target, applied\n\n`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`; HD Humanoids at size 1.0-1.42 (the boss 2.0), every character dressed (outfit `shirt`\njerseys, `sleeves: 'short'`, hair, headgear, a real palette); `propSize: 1.3`; textured floors (`floorTex`) and walls\n(`face`, `roof`); 3-8 props per screen (corner flags, the dugouts' benches, water bottles on the touchline, kit bags,\ncones, floodlight towers, sponsor boards, the sin bin, cameramen on the touchline as small Humanoids with a box camera);\neffects on every hit; `E.font.title` logos with 3-4 colour gradients and depth; light in every night scene; portraits in\nevery dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\nnot with NES ones. Performance is out of scope (TASK.md): favour detail (full crowds, lights, particles, shadows) over\nframe rate.\n\n### 10.2 Characters\n\nColours shaded with `E.tones` where drawn by hand. Each team's players differ in build, size, hair, skin and headgear so\nthey read as people, not clones; jersey colours carry the team. Mud builds up on kits at Muddington (`rig.C.cloth` and\n`pants` mixed toward `#5a3a1e` by `mud` 0-0.6, restored at the next match). Stunned players get orbiting stars (a\nthree-frame string sprite) over their heads. The ball carrier gets a subtle white outline in busy moments.\n\n### 10.3 New art assets (all drawn by code)\n\n| Asset | How |\n|---|---|\n| Oval ball (laces, panel lines; 16 turns) | `E.sprite` strings 9x6, drawn with `rot` (cached), end-over-end flicker for kicks |\n| Goalposts with pads, crossbar | `r.queue` lines and rects projected with `r.w`, depth-sorted with the ball |\n| Pitch markings, in-goal crest | `floorTex` |\n| Stands, crowd, flags, banners | TileMap tiers + `r.queue` figures (as the sports kit), `banner` props in team colours |\n| Sponsor boards with text | south boards as cut walls with text drawn on their faces through `r.queue` |\n| Floodlight towers, jumbotron (shows score, portraits, TRY!) | custom shapes (`docs/ASSETS.md` format) or `r.queue` boxes; the jumbotron draws `rig.drawPortrait` |\n| Skylines per venue | the TileMap has `outside: false`; each draw paints `r.sky([...])`, then the venue's silhouettes (hills, cranes, chimneys, towers) anchored to the far stand's projected top edge (`r.w` of its back corners), then the map, so the stand meets the skyline whatever the camera does |\n| Sin bin dumpster | a custom shape (green metal box, lid, SIN BIN stencil); the binned player drawn inside |\n| Kicking tee, cones, tackle bags, corner flags, water bottles, kit bags | small custom shapes or string sprites |\n| Power-up sprites (pie, pads, boot, jersey, horn) | string sprites 12-14 px with a glint |\n| Captain Clucky | an `E.Blob` (`R: 14`, white and yellow, `wings`, `feet`, a red comb and beak drawn over it) |\n| Flame grates and jets, scorch decals, lightning bolt | decals, `particles.fire`, `px.line` zig-zags, emissive queue items |\n| Crests (5 teams), the Channel Thud bug, the MEGA CUP trophy | string sprites and a custom shape |\n| Button badges (PlayStation, Xbox, keycaps, mouse) | string sprites (§6.4) |\n| Clubhouse, tunnel, podium sets | small TileMaps with store props (`kenney-furniture`, `kaykit-restaurant-bits` via `E.addAssets`; check with `tools/asset-find.mjs`) |\n\n### 10.4 Effects\n\nTackles: dust (`particles.dust`), grass divots (`bits` in greens), mud splats (`bits` browns) at Muddington. Big hits:\n`game.hitFx` (no damage number: leave `damage` out and check none shows), `freeze(.08)`, `shake(4)`, sparks. Monster\nhits: `freeze(.12)`, `flash`, `shake(6)`, a ring, a 1.1x zoom punch tweened back, a \"WHUMP\" text particle. Tries:\nconfetti `bits` in the scorers' colours, crowd jump, fireworks at night (`particles.explosion` high in the sky),\nlasers at the Megadome. ON FIRE and supers: `fire` particles trailing, emissive glow. Weather from `game.weather`.\n\n### 10.5 HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n\n| Where | What |\n|---|---|\n| Top left | The TV score bug: crests, three-letter names (MUD, BAD, GUL, IRN, MEG), scores, the half and the sevens clock (with HOOTER flashing past time); each team's HYPE bar under its name (flashing \"△ SUPER\" when full); sin-bin timers as small dumpster icons with seconds |\n| Top centre | Event banners (`E.font.title` scale 3-4, popped in with a tween, 1.2-2 s): TRY!, MONSTER HIT!, LINE BREAK!, ON FIRE!, SIN BIN!, REF DOWN!, PUSHOVER TRY!, DROP GOAL!, CONVERTED!, WIDE!, KNOCK-ON, FORWARD!, ADVANTAGE, HOOTER! |\n| Top right | The radar: the pitch small, dots in team colours, white ball, controlled players ringed |\n| Bottom corners | One card per human seat: the controlled player's live portrait, nickname, turbo bar, power-up icon and seconds |\n| Bottom centre | Context prompts (two or three badges with a word: \"{b:x} STEP  {b:sq} FEND  {b:ci} KICK\"), above the commentary lower-third |\n| In the world | Seat rings and chevrons; L1 / R1 badges over the two receivers; the landing ring of every kick; offside lines (dashed, team colour, \"OFFSIDE\" at the ends) during rucks, scrums and lineouts; the ref's sight cone; the \"USE IT\" ring; off-screen arrows (`r.marker`) for the ball and each controlled player |\n| Set pieces | Big centred widgets: the scrum's SET ring and push bar (with both teams' colours), the lineout's three pod buttons and the throw needle, the kick meter (vertical, with the sweet band), the set kick's reticle and wind arrow, the penalty choice's three cards |\n\n### 10.6 Menus and screens: 10-foot rules\n\n- Everything readable at 3 m on a TV: body text never below the 5x7 font at scale 1 on the ps1 buffer (about 30 TV\n  pixels high at 1080p); menu entries at scale 2; titles 3-4. No more than seven choices on a screen, and no tables of\n  numbers: results show four big numbers, team cards three bars.\n- Focus is unmistakable (a glowing box, ▸ markers, a sound); d-pad and stick move it, ✕ picks, ○ goes back; the mouse\n  over an item moves the focus, a click picks it (E.Menu does both); every card-style screen does the same with\n  `input.pointer()` / `input.clicked()`.\n- The standard HTML pause, settings and controls screens (engine's `E.Shell`) stay (they are the engine's standard\n  features), restyled for a TV with CSS in the page: `.esh { font-size: 20px }`, `.esh button { font-size: 18px;\n  padding: 14px 20px; min-height: 56px }`, `.esh-mod { width: min(720px, 100%) }`, `.esh h2 { font-size: 34px }`,\n  `.esh-row { padding: 12px 0 }`, the theme in team colours (accent `#f0c040`, paper `rgba(16,20,28,.92)`).\n- Every screen shows its prompts with the badges of the device used last.\n\n### 10.7 Camera direction (TV flourishes)\n\nWalk-outs before kick-off (both teams jog out of the tunnel to the halfway line; captains shake hands; 6 s, skippable);\na slow push-in on the kicker before a set kick; the replay angle; the crowd and jumbotron cut-ins at scores (a 1 s\npicture-in-picture of the scorer's portrait on the jumbotron); the camera never shakes during menus.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Animation\n\n### 11.1 How (native system, extended)\n\n- Everything is the engine's Humanoid rig, driven by continuous values (`rig.update(dt, state)`).\n- **Paired and multi-body moves** are `E.ACTIONS` entries (`{ beats, setup, at }` like the engine's `takedown`), run by\n  `new E.Action(name, { body, other })`; the action moves the bodies and gives `rigState()` / `otherState()`.\n- **New poses** are `rig.solvePose` wrappers that move joints after the base solve (as Emberdeep does): the ball carry,\n  arms-out celebrations, the scrum bind, the lineout lift, the referee's signals.\n- **New strikes** are attack specs in the `E.MOVES` format with `hand`, `kick`, `lunge`, `hop`, `crouch`, `lean`,\n  `twist`, `blade: 0`.\n- **The anim record:** each player's `anim` in `MatchState` is what the rig needs, compactly: `{ m (move id), ph\n  (phase), u, p (pose id), dn (down 0-1), air, fl (flip 0-1), cr (crouch), ex (expression), hu (hurt), arms (custom pose\n  id), w (pose weight) }`. The host and replays fill it from actions; online clients and replays feed it to rigs. A\n  player who is just running has no `anim` beyond velocity (the gait comes from `vx, vy`).\n- Check every new move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` contact sheets (wind-up, strike, follow-through, clean settle) and with\n  `rig.debug(r)` and `game.timeScale = .25`.\n\n### 11.2 The rugby move set\n\n| Move | Built as |\n|---|---|\n| Carry | `solvePose` wrap: the ball arm's hand at the far hip, elbow tucked; two hands on the ball when a pass is coming (the last 0.2 s before the pass button is likely, i.e. when a receiver is lined up) |\n| Pass (short, long) | a spec: `hand: 'both'`, a swing across the body from the far hip to the receiver's side at chest height, `twist`, `wind .06 active .08 recover .18`; long: bigger wind and twist |\n| Offload | a one-handed pop (`hand: 'L'`, short) while falling in the tackle |\n| Dummy | the pass spec stopped at the end of the wind, then the carry |\n| Sidestep | a lateral hop (`hop`), the body leaning away, the legs crossing (velocity impulse) |\n| Spin | `spin: true` with the ball held in both hands, `blade: 0` |\n| Fend | `thrust` with `hand: 'L'`, `blade: 0`, held (`hold .6`), stiff arm at shoulder height |\n| Tackle (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.tackle`: beats lunge .12, wrap .15, fall .35, ground .3: the tackler drives low (crouch, lean) with arms wrapping the carrier's waist; both go down (`down` 0→1), the carrier back or sideways; dust |\n| Big hit (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.bigHit`: charge .1, impact .06, launch .5, land .3: the carrier flies (an arc, `flip` 0→1), lands heavily (`land: 1`), slides; the hitter stands over him with a flex (`pose: 'guard'`, `expr: 'shout'`) |\n| Dive tackle (paired) | `E.ACTIONS.diveTackle`: the diver flies flat (`down: 1` with `z` above the ground: a superman dive), arms forward; the carrier trips and falls forward |\n| Try dive | `E.ACTIONS.tryDive`: the carrier dives flat with the ball held out, slides 12 u on the grass, a puff of dust |\n| Get up | the engine's `getUp` |\n| Ruck | bodies bent at the hips (`crouch`, a lean), heads down, legs churning (`run: 1`), one or two lying in it (`down: .6`); a dust cloud over the pile |\n| Scrum | three a side bound in a row (`solvePose`: arms over the neighbours' shoulders), bent flat-backed, `run` in place while pushing; a collapse is `down: 1` |\n| Lineout lift (three bodies) | the jumper rises to z 60 with arms up (`pose: 'cheer'` blend), two lifters crouched below with arms up holding (`pose: 'cast'` with the hands raised); timed together by one action on the jumper and one on each lifter |\n| Lineout throw | a two-handed overhead throw (`hand: 'both'`, from behind the head) |\n| Catch high ball | `air` with arms up |\n| Punt, grubber, drop kick | the engine's `kick` with the ball drawn from the hands to the foot through the wind-up; the drop kick bounces the ball once first |\n| Place kick | three run-up steps on an angle, the `kick` with a big lean and follow-through (`hold .8`); the kicker's crouched pre-kick stance beforehand |\n| Celebrations (one per player, from a pool of six) | knee slide (`down: .4` travelling), aeroplane arms (`solvePose` arms out, banking), the flex (`pose: 'guard'`, `expr: 'shout'`), the cocky one (`pose: 'hips'`), the bow, the belly flop (`down: 1` with a bounce) |\n| Referee signals | try (arm up, pointing down), penalty (arm out and up toward the team), advantage (arm out flat, held), scrum (arm out low), the card held high (a yellow or red rect at `rig.hand('R')`), the whistle at the mouth |\n| Stunned, toasted, zapped | `hurt`, a head sway (`solvePose` small roll), stars; toasted: colours darkened briefly, smoke; zapped: the skeleton rig drawn for two frames |\n| Sin bin sulk | inside the dumpster, `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'angry'` |\n| Walk-out and handshake | a jog; captains shake hands (`solvePose`: right hands meet) |\n\n---\n\n## 12. Audio (all in code: the engine's chip synth and Web Audio; no files)\n\n### 12.1 Music (song objects for `game.audio.music`, with named layers for `audio.layer`)\n\n| Song | Where | Character | Layers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"Thugby Turbo!\" | title, menus | glam-rock stomp, 152 bpm, square lead, saw bass, handclaps; the crowd chants \"THUG-BY!\" on the 2 and 4 | `base`, `chant` |\n| \"Mud and Glory\" | Muddington | brass-band march on pulses, 126 bpm | `base`, `drums` (in when the ball is in an opponents' 22), `hype` (a team's meter full / ON FIRE) |\n| \"Grumble Shanty\" | Port Grumble | a shanty in a rolling 6/8 feel (steps: 3), accordion-ish pulse12 | same three |\n| \"Forge Floor\" | The Furnace | industrial: low saw ostinato, anvil hits (noise + triangle ping), 132 bpm | same three |\n| \"Megadome Mayhem\" | the final | minor-key, fast drums, arpeggios, 160 bpm | same three |\n| \"Half-Time Pub Piano\" | halftime, clubhouse | honky-tonk, triangle + pulse | none |\n| \"Third Half\" | credits | the club song, a babble choir over it | none |\n| Stings (`audio.sting`) | | try fanfare; monster-hit brass stab; ON FIRE riff; yellow-card sad trombone; drop-goal ding-dong; victory jingle; defeat jingle; kick-off drum roll | |\n\n### 12.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices)\n\nWhistle (short, long, triple for full time), the HOOTER (a loud square and saw blare), tackle thud (low sine + noise),\nbig-hit crunch (noise burst + falling sine + boom), pass whoosh, catch slap, punt thump, grubber tap, ball bounce (a\nhollow \"bok\": triangle 300→180), DOINK (triangle 1200 ringing), scrum engage crunch, ruck grunts (babble), air horn\n(square chord), pie munch, turbo whoosh and sputter, super charge (a rising arpeggio), flame jet roar (filtered noise\nsweep), lightning crack and thunder, chicken squawk (square, vibrato up and down), mud squelch, card ding and the crowd\nboo, the slow hand-clap, menu select/confirm/cancel (engine presets).\n\n### 12.3 Voices: Animalese-style babble\n\n- Patch 4 gives `E.Dialog.onLetter(ch, i, text)`. `TT.babble.letter(ch, speaker)` plays one syllable per letter: letters\n  map to semitone offsets (vowels lower and 30% longer), `freq = speaker.base × 2^(semi/12)`, a 45-75 ms voice of the\n  speaker's wave (`sfx({ wave, freq, to: freq × 0.94, dur, vol, vib })`), louder and higher for capitals, a rise over the\n  last three letters before `?`, a jump on `!`; spaces and punctuation are silent beats.\n- Speakers: Barry (square, base 330, fast), Ros (triangle, 220, measured), Gristle (saw, 140, gravel: a second voice an\n  octave down), Nigel (pulse12, 260, nasal), Big Dave (triangle, 160), each player (pitch from size and build:\n  80-300), Nan (pulse, 380 with vibrato), Sir Rupert (square, 200, slow), Big Unit (saw, 70, one roar), the stadium PA\n  (square, 180, with an echo: the same syllable 180 ms later at half volume).\n- In play: players grunt short babble bursts on tackles, rucks and scrums; the referee babbles his calls; the crowd\n  chants in a choir of five detuned voices on the beat (`audio.onBeat`).\n\n### 12.4 The crowd\n\nA looping bed of filtered noise whose volume follows excitement (ball near a try line, a line break, a big hit) with\nswells, roars on scores, a groan on misses, boos on cards, the slow hand-clap at set kicks; a Crowd volume slider in\nSound.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Attract mode\n\n- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it. One `new E.Arcade(game, { id:\n  'thugby', idle: 10, demo: 300, scores: 8, hud: false })`; those scenes call `arcade.attract(dt)` each step; when\n  `arcade.phase` turns `'demo'` they `game.go('match', { attract: true })`; the director calls `arcade.endDemo()` and\n  goes back to the title at its end (the `'scores'` phase then shows the records with `arcade.drawTable`); an exit by\n  input calls `arcade.wake()`. Our own idle check (below) also counts mouse movement and sticks.\n- It is a CPU vs CPU match (teams and venue rotate through all four venues across loops) with cheats on: no clock,\n  hype on demand, events forced. A **director** (`game.script`) walks a showcase list, using the same `game.debug.force`\n  calls as the dev panel, each step when the previous one finished (or 12 s passed):\n  1. walk-out and kick-off; 2. a run with a sidestep and a fend; 3. a pass chain along the line with a dummy; 4. a\n  MONSTER HIT and its replay; 5. a ruck with a jackal; 6. a knock-on and a scrum; 7. a kick to touch and a lineout; 8. a\n  power-up thrown on and taken; 9. the venue's hazard; 10. THUNDER RUN to a try, the celebration, the replay; 11. the\n  conversion in the kicker's camera; 12. a cheap shot behind the ref's back, then one he sees: a yellow card and the sin\n  bin; 13. a player ON FIRE scoring; 14. a drop goal. Then the logo and the records for 8 s, then the title.\n- Overlays: \"DEMO\" top centre, a blinking \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (or \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" on touch-only), the\n  logo small in a corner; the HUD and commentary as in a real match.\n- Any input exits at once: a key, a mouse button or movement over 8 px, a pad button or a stick past 0.5, a tap. The\n  exiting input is consumed (`consumeAll`) so it does not also pick a menu item. It returns to the title.\n- Attract never writes saves or records and never runs in an AI Hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Dev mode","numLines":400,"startLine":920,"totalLines":1679}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MKRsnchjxCqAi1JEf1owSW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
