{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8jvZr7vu7t98ZcbRC95ng","type":"tool_result","content":"// Usage:  node tools/filmstrip.mjs game.html[?query][#scene] --steps \"<steps>\" [--out strip.png] [--cols 8] [--scale 2] [--crop x,y,w,h]\n//                                  [--seed 1] [--hz 60] [--compare other.html[#scene]]\n//   rec:16:2          start recording 16 frames, one every 2 display frames (runs alongside the next steps)\n// up with whole pixels; --crop takes a region of that buffer (in game pixels) to zoom on one character.\n// --seed N makes the run repeatable: time is virtual (every display frame is exactly 1/60 s, and wait:600 runs\n// pixel for pixel, on any machine. Use it whenever two strips will be compared. --hz 144 makes the virtual display run at\n// another refresh rate (frames of exactly 1/144 s; it implies --seed): the clock's steps per frame show on the strip.\n// --compare b.html records the same steps from a second page (another build, or the game after your change) and\n// lays the strips out A above B, with a third row that marks every pixel that differs. It implies --seed (1 if\n// --expect-same (with --compare) exits with code 1 when any frame differs: tools/determinism-test.mjs compares a page with\n// itself this way, to prove the same steps give the same pixels.\n// Example: node tools/filmstrip.mjs dist/my-3d2dge.html#brawler --steps \"wait:1500 press:Enter wait:800 rec:16:2 press:KeyJ wait:120 press:KeyJ\" --out jab.png","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b392508-0a9c-4851-a1e8-b9fce2e4b886","uuid":"e0599310-9f61-42ec-9402-4be600971002","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:29:45.716Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// Usage:  node tools/filmstrip.mjs game.html[?query][#scene] --steps \"<steps>\" [--out strip.png] [--cols 8] [--scale 2] [--crop x,y,w,h]\n//                                  [--seed 1] [--hz 60] [--compare other.html[#scene]]\n//   rec:16:2          start recording 16 frames, one every 2 display frames (runs alongside the next steps)\n// up with whole pixels; --crop takes a region of that buffer (in game pixels) to zoom on one character.\n// --seed N makes the run repeatable: time is virtual (every display frame is exactly 1/60 s, and wait:600 runs\n// pixel for pixel, on any machine. Use it whenever two strips will be compared. --hz 144 makes the virtual display run at\n// another refresh rate (frames of exactly 1/144 s; it implies --seed): the clock's steps per frame show on the strip.\n// --compare b.html records the same steps from a second page (another build, or the game after your change) and\n// lays the strips out A above B, with a third row that marks every pixel that differs. It implies --seed (1 if\n// --expect-same (with --compare) exits with code 1 when any frame differs: tools/determinism-test.mjs compares a page with\n// itself this way, to prove the same steps give the same pixels.\n// Example: node tools/filmstrip.mjs dist/my-3d2dge.html#brawler --steps \"wait:1500 press:Enter wait:800 rec:16:2 press:KeyJ wait:120 press:KeyJ\" --out jab.png","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K8jvZr7vu7t98ZcbRC95ng","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
